{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N8ynZbU4ckA6Zo2afTuBLc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '原始 \"Likert Blindspot\" framing 完全成立。 C2 是 primary contribution：exp-010\n2\t  binarized Likert sign test 不显著 (p=0.24)，确认 gap 是 measurement 结构差异而非统计检验选择差异。3 个\n3\t  judge × 3 个 benchmark 中 7/9 组合出现 Likert-Pairwise gap， 无 reverse pattern。C1 作为 application\n4\t  contribution 诚实定位，组件来源全部 acknowledge。 C3 降级为 preliminary：formality robust + register\n5\t  作为第二 working axis + tone/verbosity 作为 principled boundary。C4 通过 logistic regression\n6\t  (exp-014) formality 主效应独立显著 (p=0.006) 提供 CSD-adjusted win rate 的统计基础。n=500 复制 (exp-006)\n7\t  消除 sample size 质疑。 NLI threshold sensitivity (exp-011) 证明结果在 70%-95% 范围内 robust。\n8\t  Human validation (exp-013) κ=0.72 证明 NLI gate 不是 black box。 Headline: \"Standard\n9\t  Likert scoring misses style bias that pairwise comparison detects across 3 judges\n10\t  and 3 benchmarks — a structural measurement limitation, not a statistical artifact,\n11\t  confirmed by binarized Likert control.\" Main result table 中 binarized Likert 列提供\n12\t  C2 决定性证据。 25+ refs 到位，projected review score 4.0-4.5，直冲 Main。\n13\t\n14\t  '\n15\timagined_experiments:\n16\t- name: Multi-judge formality pairwise\n17\t  plan_id: exp-001\n18\t  description: '在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 formality pairwise 实验。\n19\t    使用已生成的 counterfactual pairs (n=100)，每个 judge 做 dual-direction pairwise， position\n20\t    control。与 GPT-4o baseline (69.1%, p=0.006) 对比。\n21\t\n22\t    '\n23\t  expected_results:\n24\t    gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.691\n25\t    gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.006\n26\t    gpt4o_n_consistent: 55\n27\t    gpt4o_formal_wins: 38\n28\t    gpt4o_casual_wins: 17\n29\t    claude_sonnet_formal_win_rate: 0.64\n30\t    claude_sonnet_sign_test_p: 0.028\n31\t    claude_sonnet_n_consistent: 50\n32\t    claude_sonnet_formal_wins: 32\n33\t    claude_sonnet_casual_wins: 18\n34\t    claude_sonnet_consistency_rate: 0.51\n35\t    gemini_flash_formal_win_rate: 0.724\n36\t    gemini_flash_sign_test_p: 0.002\n37\t    gemini_flash_n_consistent: 58\n38\t    gemini_flash_formal_wins: 42\n39\t    gemini_flash_casual_wins: 16\n40\t    gemini_flash_consistency_rate: 0.59\n41\t    n_judges_significant_after_holm: 3\n42\t    holm_corrected_p_values:\n43\t      gemini: 0.006\n44\t      gpt4o: 0.012\n45\t      claude: 0.028\n46\t    cross_judge_mean_winrate: 0.685\n47\t    cross_judge_winrate_range:\n48\t    - 0.64\n49\t    - 0.724\n50\t    cross_judge_pairwise_p_median: 0.006\n51\t  result_rationale: 'Formality bias 是 LLM judge 的通用现象而非 GPT-4o 特有。三个 judge 的 RLHF\n52\t    训练数据 普遍偏向 formal/professional 风格回答，formal text 与 higher-quality content 在 pretraining\n53\t    语料中高度相关。Claude-Sonnet 效应略弱 (0.64) 因为 Anthropic 的 RLHF 有更多 helpfulness 导向校准，对 surface\n54\t    style 依赖稍低；Gemini-Flash 效应略强 (0.72) 因为轻量模型更依赖 surface heuristics 作为 quality proxy。三者量级差异\n55\t    (0.64-0.72) 本身也是 C3 evidence—— bias magnitude 是 judge-dependent 的。Holm correction\n56\t    后全部 p<0.05，因为每个 judge 的 raw p 都足够小 (最大 0.028)，3 重比较惩罚不足以翻转。\n57\t\n58\t    '\n59\t  tables:\n60\t  - title: 'Table 2: Formality Pairwise Results Across Judges (LLMBar, n=100)'\n61\t    columns:\n62\t    - Judge\n63\t    - n_consistent\n64\t    - Formal Wins\n65\t    - Casual Wins\n66\t    - Win Rate\n67\t    - 95% CI\n68\t    - Sign Test p\n69\t    - Holm p\n70\t    rows:\n71\t    - - GPT-4o\n72\t      - 55\n73\t      - 38\n74\t      - 17\n75\t      - 69.1%\n76\t      - '[56.0%, 79.7%]'\n77\t      - 0.006**\n78\t      - 0.012*\n79\t    - - Claude-Sonnet\n80\t      - 50\n81\t      - 32\n82\t      - 18\n83\t      - 64.0%\n84\t      - '[50.1%, 75.9%]'\n85\t      - 0.028*\n86\t      - 0.028*\n87\t    - - Gemini-Flash\n88\t      - 58\n89\t      - 42\n90\t      - 16\n91\t      - 72.4%\n92\t      - '[59.8%, 82.3%]'\n93\t      - 0.002**\n94\t      - 0.006**\n95\t  figures_description:\n96\t  - 'Figure 3 (partial): 3×3 heatmap 的 LLMBar 列。色阶从 50% (neutral) 到 75% (strong bias)，\n97\t    三个 judge 均深色，视觉化 cross-judge 一致性。\n98\t\n99\t    '\n100\t  analysis: 'A1 假设成立：3/3 judge 在 Holm correction 后显著。cross_judge_mean_winrate 0.685\n101\t    在 [0.60, 0.75] 范围中上。Judge 间量级差异 (Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude) 稳定， 为 C3 axis-dependency\n102\t    提供 judge 维度证据。Direction asymmetry 在所有 judge 上存在 (formal-original 方向更强)，为 exp-005\n103\t    original preference 控制提供动机。\n104\t\n105\t    '\n106\t- name: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\n107\t  plan_id: exp-002\n108\t  description: '在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上运行 CSD 流程。新 counterfactual generation (不同\n109\t    source text)。 三个 judge (GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash) 分别评测。每个 benchmark\n110\t    n=100。 与 LLMBar 结果交叉比较，形成 3×3 矩阵。\n111\t\n112\t    '\n113\t  expected_results:\n114\t    alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.67\n115\t    alpacaeval_gpt4o_p: 0.012\n116\t    alpacaeval_claude_formal_winrate: 0.61\n117\t    alpacaeval_claude_p: 0.048\n118\t    alpacaeval_gemini_formal_winrate: 0.7\n119\t    alpacaeval_gemini_p: 0.004\n120\t    alpacaeval_counterfactual_nli_pass: 0.9\n121\t    alpacaeval_nli_mean: 0.908\n122\t    mtbench_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.65\n123\t    mtbench_gpt4o_p: 0.018\n124\t    mtbench_claude_formal_winrate: 0.6\n125\t    mtbench_claude_p: 0.065\n126\t    mtbench_gemini_formal_winrate: 0.68\n127\t    mtbench_gemini_p: 0.008\n128\t    mtbench_counterfactual_nli_pass: 0.87\n129\t    mtbench_nli_mean: 0.882\n130\t    n_benchmarks_with_gap: 3\n131\t    significant_combos_total: 7\n132\t    total_combos: 9\n133\t    non_significant_combos:\n134\t    - Claude×MT-Bench (p=0.065, borderline)\n135\t    borderline_combos: 1\n136\t    mean_winrate_across_all_9: 0.664\n137\t  result_rationale: 'Formality bias 跨 benchmark 泛化，因为 bias 源于 judge 内在偏好而非特定数据集特征。\n138\t    AlpacaEval 效应略强于 MT-Bench：open-ended instruction-following 任务给 style variation\n139\t    更大空间，formal tone 作为 quality proxy 权重更大；MT-Bench 的 multi-turn 结构和更 specific 的评判标准\n140\t    (如 math/reasoning accuracy) 部分抑制了 style 影响。Claude×MT-Bench 是唯一 borderline 不显著的组合\n141\t    (p=0.065)，因为 Claude 在有明确正确性标准的 benchmark 上更倾向 content-based 判断，且 Claude 本身 formality\n142\t    sensitivity 最低。NLI pass rate 在 AlpacaEval (0.90) 略高于 MT-Bench (0.87)，因为 AlpacaEval\n143\t    response 结构更简单， counterfactual 改写更容易保持语义。7/9 显著远超偶然水平。\n144\t\n145\t    '\n146\t  tables:\n147\t  - title: 'Table 3: Formality Pairwise Win Rate Matrix (Judge × Benchmark)'\n148\t    columns:\n149\t    - Judge\n150\t    - LLMBar\n151\t    - AlpacaEval\n152\t    - MT-Bench\n153\t    - Mean\n154\t    rows:\n155\t    - - GPT-4o\n156\t      - 69.1%**\n157\t      - 67.0%*\n158\t      - 65.0%*\n159\t      - 67.0%\n160\t    - - Claude-Sonnet\n161\t      - 64.0%*\n162\t      - 61.0%*\n163\t      - 60.0%†\n164\t      - 61.7%\n165\t    - - Gemini-Flash\n166\t      - 72.4%**\n167\t      - 70.0%**\n168\t      - 68.0%**\n169\t      - 70.1%\n170\t    - - Mean\n171\t      - 68.5%\n172\t      - 66.0%\n173\t      - 64.3%\n174\t      - 66.3%\n175\t    footnote: '** p<0.01, * p<0.05, † p<0.10. n=100 per cell, n_consistent varies\n176\t      48-58.'\n177\t  - title: 'Table 4: Counterfactual Quality per Benchmark'\n178\t    columns:\n179\t    - Benchmark\n180\t    - n\n181\t    - NLI Pass Rate\n182\t    - NLI Mean\n183\t    - BERTScore Mean\n184\t    rows:\n185\t    - - LLMBar\n186\t      - 100\n187\t      - 88%\n188\t      - 0.896\n189\t      - 0.842\n190\t    - - AlpacaEval\n191\t      - 100\n192\t      - 90%\n193\t      - 0.908\n194\t      - 0.851\n195\t    - - MT-Bench\n196\t      - 100\n197\t      - 87%\n198\t      - 0.882\n199\t      - 0.835\n200\t  figures_description:\n201\t  - 'Figure 3 (main): 3 judges × 3 benchmarks heatmap，cell 内标注 win rate 和显著性星号。 色阶：50%=白色,\n202\t    60%=浅蓝, 70%=深蓝, 80%=深色。视觉传达 cross-judge × cross-benchmark 一致的 formality premium。唯一浅色\n203\t    cell 是 Claude×MT-Bench (60.0%†)。\n204\t\n205\t    '\n206\t  analysis: 'A2 假设成立：3/3 benchmarks 显示 gap。Benchmark 梯度 (LLMBar > AlpacaEval > MT-Bench)\n207\t    有方法论意义——task-specific evaluation criteria 越强，style bias 越被抑制。 Judge 梯度 (Gemini\n208\t    > GPT-4o > Claude) 稳定跨 benchmark，说明 judge 的 style sensitivity 是其内在属性而非 benchmark\n209\t    artifact。9 个组合的 mean win rate 0.664 在 cross_judge_formal_win_rate [0.60, 0.75]\n210\t    范围内。\n211\t\n212\t    '\n213\t- name: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\n214\t  plan_id: exp-003\n215\t  description: '对 exp-001/002 的每个 judge×benchmark 组合，计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win\n216\t    rate， 系统性比较两种 measurement 的 sensitivity。同一 counterfactual 数据。\n217\t\n218\t    '\n219\t  expected_results:\n220\t    llmbar_gpt4o_likert_ate: 0.1\n221\t    llmbar_gpt4o_likert_p: 0.332\n222\t    llmbar_gpt4o_pairwise_p: 0.006\n223\t    llmbar_claude_likert_ate: 0.06\n224\t    llmbar_claude_likert_p: 0.485\n225\t    llmbar_claude_pairwise_p: 0.028\n226\t    llmbar_gemini_likert_ate: 0.14\n227\t    llmbar_gemini_likert_p: 0.198\n228\t    llmbar_gemini_pairwise_p: 0.002\n229\t    alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_ate: 0.08\n230\t    alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_p: 0.412\n231\t    alpacaeval_claude_likert_ate: 0.04\n232\t    alpacaeval_claude_likert_p: 0.551\n233\t    alpacaeval_gemini_likert_ate: 0.12\n234\t    alpacaeval_gemini_likert_p: 0.142\n235\t    mtbench_gpt4o_likert_ate: 0.09\n236\t    mtbench_gpt4o_likert_p: 0.388\n237\t    mtbench_claude_likert_ate: 0.03\n238\t    mtbench_claude_likert_p: 0.612\n239\t    mtbench_gemini_likert_ate: 0.11\n240\t    mtbench_gemini_likert_p: 0.175\n241\t    combos_with_gap: 7\n242\t    combos_without_gap: 2\n243\t    combos_total: 9\n244\t    gap_note: 2 个无 gap：Claude×MT-Bench (两者都不显著，一致性 non-sig)，Gemini×AlpacaEval Likert\n245\t      p=0.142 borderline\n246\t    median_likert_p: 0.388\n247\t    median_pairwise_p: 0.012\n248\t    cross_judge_likert_ate_p_median: 0.37\n249\t    no_reverse_pattern: true\n250\t  result_rationale: 'Likert-Pairwise gap 的根因是 measurement scale 的信息结构差异。Likert pointwise\n251\t    评分中， style bias 被三个机制稀释：(1) score anchoring——judge 倾向使用量表中段，微小 style 偏好 不足以跨越\n252\t    score boundary；(2) absolute calibration noise——不同 item 的 baseline quality 差异远大于\n253\t    style 引入的差异，between-item variance 淹没 within-item style effect； (3) 离散量表的 resolution\n254\t    limit——1-10 scale 上 0.10 的 ATE 被四舍五入吸收。 Pairwise 直接呈现 A/B 对比，消除 absolute calibration\n255\t    问题，将 style 差异放大为 forced choice 中的 tie-breaking signal。Gemini 的 Likert p (0.142-0.198)\n256\t    最接近显著， 因为 Gemini 的 formality premium 最强 (72.4%)，即使 Likert 的稀释也无法完全消除。 但仍未达 p<0.05，确认\n257\t    Likert blindspot 的系统性。\n258\t\n259\t    '\n260\t  tables:\n261\t  - title: 'Table 5: Likert ATE vs Pairwise Win Rate — The Likert Blindspot'\n262\t    columns:\n263\t    - Judge × Benchmark\n264\t    - Likert ATE\n265\t    - Likert p\n266\t    - Pairwise WR\n267\t    - Pairwise p\n268\t    - Gap?\n269\t    rows:\n270\t    - - GPT-4o × LLMBar\n271\t      - '+0.10'\n272\t      - '0.332'\n273\t      - 69.1%\n274\t      - 0.006**\n275\t      - ✓\n276\t    - - Claude × LLMBar\n277\t      - '+0.06'\n278\t      - '0.485'\n279\t      - 64.0%\n280\t      - 0.028*\n281\t      - ✓\n282\t    - - Gemini × LLMBar\n283\t      - '+0.14'\n284\t      - '0.198'\n285\t      - 72.4%\n286\t      - 0.002**\n287\t      - ✓\n288\t    - - GPT-4o × AlpacaEval\n289\t      - '+0.08'\n290\t      - '0.412'\n291\t      - 67.0%\n292\t      - 0.012*\n293\t      - ✓\n294\t    - - Claude × AlpacaEval\n295\t      - '+0.04'\n296\t      - '0.551'\n297\t      - 61.0%\n298\t      - 0.048*\n299\t      - ✓\n300\t    - - Gemini × AlpacaEval\n301\t      - '+0.12'\n302\t      - '0.142'\n303\t      - 70.0%\n304\t      - 0.004**\n305\t      - ✓\n306\t    - - GPT-4o × MT-Bench\n307\t      - '+0.09'\n308\t      - '0.388'\n309\t      - 65.0%\n310\t      - 0.018*\n311\t      - ✓\n312\t    - - Claude × MT-Bench\n313\t      - '+0.03'\n314\t      - '0.612'\n315\t      - 60.0%\n316\t      - 0.065†\n317\t      - —\n318\t    - - Gemini × MT-Bench\n319\t      - '+0.11'\n320\t      - '0.175'\n321\t      - 68.0%\n322\t      - 0.008**\n323\t      - ✓\n324\t    footnote: Gap = Likert p>0.10 AND Pairwise p<0.05. 7/9 combos show gap. 0/9 reverse\n325\t      pattern.\n326\t  figures_description:\n327\t  - 'Figure 1 (main, problem illustration): 双面板对比图。左: Likert ATE 带 95% CI error bar，\n328\t    所有 9 个组合 CI 均跨零线。右: Pairwise win rate 带 Wilson CI，7/9 CI 不含 50%。 视觉冲击力：同一数据、两种\n329\t    measurement、截然不同的结论。\n330\t\n331\t    '\n332\t  analysis: 'C2 的核心 evidence。7/9 组合出现系统性 measurement gap，且无 reverse pattern (没有任何组合\n333\t    Likert 显著但 Pairwise 不显著)。median Likert p = 0.37 在 [0.15, 0.5] 范围内， median Pairwise\n334\t    p = 0.012 在 [0.001, 0.02] 范围内。gap 不依赖特定 judge 或 benchmark—— 这意味着现有文献中基于 Likert\n335\t    的 style bias 研究可能系统性低估问题严重程度。 Practical implication: style bias audit 应使用 pairwise\n336\t    comparison 而非 pointwise scoring。\n337\t\n338\t    '\n339\t- name: Tone axis (assertive/hedging) — negative control\n340\t  plan_id: exp-004\n341\t  description: 'D014 Tone pilot 已失败 (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%)。Epistemic commitment\n342\t    change 与 NLI verification 结构性不兼容。本实验以 pilot 数据 (n=20) 为基础，正式文档化失败模式， 作为 C3 的 axis\n343\t    boundary evidence。不需额外 API 调用。\n344\t\n345\t    '\n346\t  expected_results:\n347\t    n_pilot: 20\n348\t    nli_cf_pass_rate: 0.65\n349\t    nli_cf_mean: 0.704\n350\t    bertscore_cf_mean: 0.92\n351\t    joint_pass_rate: 0.45\n352\t    by_tone_assertive_both_pass: 0.385\n353\t    by_tone_hedging_both_pass: 0.571\n354\t    catastrophic_nli_lt001_count: 6\n355\t    catastrophic_fraction: 0.3\n356\t    failure_mode: assertive→hedging 改变 epistemic commitment (confidence markers, modal\n357\t      verbs)，NLI 正确检测为 non-entailment\n358\t    structural_incompatibility: true\n359\t    pipeline_stopped_at: content_verification\n360\t  result_rationale: 'Tone 改变 (assertive↔hedging) 不是纯 style 变换——它改变了说话者对命题的认知承诺程度。\n361\t    \"X is the best approach\" vs \"X might be a reasonable approach\" 在 NLI 框架下不构成双向蕴含，\n362\t    因为前者的 truth conditions 严格强于后者。30% 的样本出现 catastrophic NLI<0.01， 说明这不是 threshold\n363\t    选择问题而是根本性的语义兼容性问题。Hedging 方向 (assertive→hedging) both_pass 更高 (57.1% vs 38.5%)，因为弱化断言仍蕴含弱化后的命题，但强化断言\n364\t    (hedging→assertive) 引入了原文未承诺的确定性。这个不对称性本身就是 principled boundary 的证据：NLI gate 不是\n365\t    arbitrary obstacle，而是正确识别了语义改变。\n366\t\n367\t    '\n368\t  tables:\n369\t  - title: 'Table A1: Tone Axis Content Verification Failure (n=20 pilot)'\n370\t    columns:\n371\t    - Direction\n372\t    - n\n373\t    - NLI Mean\n374\t    - Both Pass Rate\n375\t    - Catastrophic NLI<0.01\n376\t    rows:\n377\t    - - Assertive→Hedging\n378\t      - 13\n379\t      - '0.656'\n380\t      - 38.5%\n381\t      - 4/13 (30.8%)\n382\t    - - Hedging→Assertive\n383\t      - 7\n384\t      - '0.793'\n385\t      - 57.1%\n386\t      - 2/7 (28.6%)\n387\t    - - Overall\n388\t      - 20\n389\t      - '0.704'\n390\t      - 45.0%\n391\t      - 6/20 (30.0%)\n392\t  figures_description:\n393\t  - 'Appendix Figure: NLI score distribution histogram for tone vs formality counterfactuals。\n394\t    Formality: 右偏，集中在 0.85-1.0。Tone: 双峰分布，一峰在 0.8-1.0 (成功保留)， 一峰在 0.0-0.1 (catastrophic\n395\t    failure)。视觉化结构性不兼容。\n396\t\n397\t    '\n398\t  analysis: 'Tone 作为 negative control 为 C3 提供 principled method boundary：CSD 适用于 不改变认知承诺的\n399\t    surface-level style axes (formality ✓)，不适用于改变 epistemic commitment 的 axes (tone\n400\t    ✗)。NLI gate 在此处正确拒绝—— 这不是方法失败，而是正确的质量控制行为。Paper 中定位为 \"method boundary\" 而非 \"negative\n401\t    result\"，因为它回答了 \"CSD 适用范围\" 这个审稿人一定会问的问题。\n402\t\n403\t    '\n404\t- name: Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\n405\t  plan_id: exp-005\n406\t  description: 'Original text vs 同风格 double-rewrite 的 pairwise 比较，量化 original preference\n407\t    confound。 D015: 扩展到所有 judge × LLMBar 组合。同时分析 casual-original subset (main pairwise\n408\t    中原文为 casual 的子集) 在不同 judge 上的 formal win rate。\n409\t\n410\t    '\n411\t  expected_results:\n412\t    gpt4o_n_valid: 95\n413\t    gpt4o_n_consistent: 60\n414\t    gpt4o_original_wins: 32\n415\t    gpt4o_rewrite_wins: 28\n416\t    gpt4o_original_win_rate: 0.533\n417\t    gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.362\n418\t    gpt4o_wilson_ci:\n419\t    - 0.408\n420\t    - 0.655\n421\t    claude_n_consistent: 55\n422\t    claude_original_wins: 28\n423\t    claude_rewrite_wins: 27\n424\t    claude_original_win_rate: 0.509\n425\t    claude_sign_test_p: 0.92\n426\t    gemini_n_consistent: 62\n427\t    gemini_original_wins: 34\n428\t    gemini_rewrite_wins: 28\n429\t    gemini_original_win_rate: 0.548\n430\t    gemini_sign_test_p: 0.28\n431\t    mean_original_win_rate: 0.53\n432\t    any_judge_original_pref_significant: false\n433\t    casual_orig_gpt4o_formal_wr: 0.545\n434\t    casual_orig_gpt4o_p: 0.832\n435\t    casual_orig_gpt4o_n: 22\n436\t    casual_orig_claude_formal_wr: 0.63\n437\t    casual_orig_claude_p: 0.072\n438\t    casual_orig_claude_n: 27\n439\t    casual_orig_gemini_formal_wr: 0.611\n440\t    casual_orig_gemini_p: 0.096\n441\t    casual_orig_gemini_n: 36\n442\t    casual_orig_best_judge: Claude\n443\t    casual_orig_best_judge_wr: 0.63\n444\t    casual_orig_best_judge_p: 0.072\n445\t  result_rationale: 'Original preference 在所有 judge 上均弱且不显著 (mean 53.0%)，因为 double-rewrite\n446\t    过程 虽引入轻微 rewrite artifact (如稍微不自然的措辞)，但这个 artifact 对 judge 影响是随机的 而非系统性的。Claude\n447\t    的 original preference 最弱 (50.9%)，可能因为 Claude 对 \"naturalness\" 的敏感度更低。Gemini 稍高\n448\t    (54.8%)，可能因为轻量模型对 fluency 微妙差异更敏感。 Casual-original subset 分析是关键：Claude 上 63.0%\n449\t    formal win rate (p=0.072) 说明即使 formality preference 与 original preference 方向相反\n450\t    (formal = rewrite)， formality 仍占上风。这在 GPT-4o 上不显著 (54.5%) 可能因为 GPT-4o 的 original\n451\t    preference (53.3%) 与 formality preference 恰好在 casual-original subset 上互相抵消。 Claude\n452\t    original preference 更弱 (50.9%)，所以 formality 更容易 dominate。\n453\t\n454\t    '\n455\t  tables:\n456\t  - title: 'Table 6: Original Preference Control Across Judges (LLMBar)'\n457\t    columns:\n458\t    - Judge\n459\t    - n_consistent\n460\t    - Original Wins\n461\t    - Rewrite Wins\n462\t    - Original WR\n463\t    - p\n464\t    rows:\n465\t    - - GPT-4o\n466\t      - 60\n467\t      - 32\n468\t      - 28\n469\t      - 53.3%\n470\t      - '0.362'\n471\t    - - Claude-Sonnet\n472\t      - 55\n473\t      - 28\n474\t      - 27\n475\t      - 50.9%\n476\t      - '0.920'\n477\t    - - Gemini-Flash\n478\t      - 62\n479\t      - 34\n480\t      - 28\n481\t      - 54.8%\n482\t      - '0.280'\n483\t  - title: 'Table 7: Casual-Original Subset — Formal Win Rate When Opposing Original\n484\t      Preference'\n485\t    columns:\n486\t    - Judge\n487\t    - n_consistent\n488\t    - Formal Wins\n489\t    - Formal WR\n490\t    - p\n491\t    rows:\n492\t    - - GPT-4o\n493\t      - 22\n494\t      - 12\n495\t      - 54.5%\n496\t      - '0.832'\n497\t    - - Claude-Sonnet\n498\t      - 27\n499\t      - 17\n500\t      - 63.0%\n501\t      - 0.072†\n502\t    - - Gemini-Flash\n503\t      - 36\n504\t      - 22\n505\t      - 61.1%\n506\t      - 0.096†\n507\t    footnote: † p<0.10. Formal = rewrite in this subset, so original preference opposes\n508\t      formality.\n509\t  figures_description:\n510\t  - 'Figure 5 (partial): Effect decomposition bar chart。三组柱状图 (GPT-4o, Claude, Gemini)，\n511\t    每组两柱：total formal WR (tall, ~65-72%) vs original preference WR (short, ~51-55%)。\n512\t    差值区间标注 \"formality-attributable effect\"。\n513\t\n514\t    '\n515\t  analysis: 'A6 假设成立：original preference 贡献 <5 个百分点 (mean 53% - 50% = 3%)， 远小于 formality\n516\t    premium (mean 68.5% - 50% = 18.5%)。Casual-original subset 在 Claude (63%) 和 Gemini\n517\t    (61.1%) 上均 >60%，best judge p=0.072 满足 p<0.10。 casual_orig_best_judge_wr 0.63 在\n518\t    [0.60, 0.70] 范围内。 Direction asymmetry (MVP 中 formal-orig 78.8% vs casual-orig\n519\t    54.5%) 主要解释 从 \"original preference\" 转向 \"改写方向的非对称难度\"。\n520\t\n521\t    '\n522\t- name: Scaled replication (n=500)\n523\t  plan_id: exp-006\n524\t  description: '将 formality pairwise 实验从 n=100 扩大到 n=500。选择效应最强的 judge×benchmark 组合\n525\t    (Gemini×LLMBar)。Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。 五个 n=100 子组的稳定性分析。\n526\t\n527\t    '\n528\t  expected_results:\n529\t    n_total: 500\n530\t    n_valid_both_trials: 490\n531\t    n_consistent: 278\n532\t    consistency_rate: 0.567\n533\t    formal_wins: 184\n534\t    casual_wins: 94\n535\t    formal_win_rate: 0.662\n536\t    wilson_ci:\n537\t    - 0.604\n538\t    - 0.716\n539\t    sign_test_p: 1.0e-05\n540\t    cohens_h: 0.337\n541\t    likert_ate_n500: 0.11\n542\t    likert_ate_p_n500: 0.082\n543\t    likert_still_borderline: true\n544\t    sub1_winrate: 0.7\n545\t    sub2_winrate: 0.65\n546\t    sub3_winrate: 0.68\n547\t    sub4_winrate: 0.64\n548\t    sub5_winrate: 0.64\n549\t    subgroup_sd: 0.026\n550\t    power_n100_d065: 0.72\n551\t    power_n300_d065: 0.97\n552\t    power_n500_d065: 0.995\n553\t    min_detectable_wr_n500: 0.56\n554\t    nli_ge90_n_consistent: 232\n555\t    nli_ge90_winrate: 0.685\n556\t    nli_ge80_n_consistent: 262\n557\t    nli_ge80_winrate: 0.668\n558\t  result_rationale: 'n=500 时 win rate 0.662 相比 n=100 pilot 的 0.691 有 2.9% 的 regression\n559\t    to mean， 这在预期范围内——pilot 的 point estimate 在 CI [0.56, 0.80] 上端，larger sample 收敛到\n560\t    true effect。CI 从 [0.56, 0.80] 收窄到 [0.60, 0.72]，p 从 0.006 降到 <0.001。 五个 n=100 子组\n561\t    win rate 在 0.64-0.70 范围波动 (σ=0.026)，展示效应高度稳定。 关键发现：即使 n=500，Likert ATE 仍仅 borderline\n562\t    显著 (p=0.082)——这强化了 C2： Likert blindspot 不是 power 问题，而是 measurement sensitivity\n563\t    的结构性差异。 如果仅仅是 power 问题，n=500 的 Likert 应当显著；它仍不显著说明 Likert 对 style bias 的检测本身就是\n564\t    structurally impaired。\n565\t\n566\t    '\n567\t  tables:\n568\t  - title: 'Table 8: Scaled Replication (Gemini × LLMBar, Formality)'\n569\t    columns:\n570\t    - Scale\n571\t    - n_consistent\n572\t    - Formal WR\n573\t    - 95% CI\n574\t    - Pairwise p\n575\t    - Likert p\n576\t    rows:\n577\t    - - n=100 (MVP pilot)\n578\t      - 55\n579\t      - 69.1%\n580\t      - '[56.0%, 79.7%]'\n581\t      - 0.006**\n582\t      - '0.332'\n583\t    - - n=500 (replication)\n584\t      - 278\n585\t      - 66.2%\n586\t      - '[60.4%, 71.6%]'\n587\t      - <0.001***\n588\t      - 0.082†\n589\t    footnote: Likert p still non-significant at n=500 (borderline), confirming structural\n590\t      measurement gap.\n591\t  - title: 'Table 9: Subgroup Stability (5 × n=100 splits)'\n592\t    columns:\n593\t    - Split\n594\t    - n_consistent\n595\t    - Formal WR\n596\t    rows:\n597\t    - - Block 1\n598\t      - 57\n599\t      - 70.0%\n600\t    - - Block 2\n601\t      - 53\n602\t      - 65.0%\n603\t    - - Block 3\n604\t      - 56\n605\t      - 68.0%\n606\t    - - Block 4\n607\t      - 54\n608\t      - 64.0%\n609\t    - - Block 5\n610\t      - 58\n611\t      - 64.0%\n612\t    - - Full n=500\n613\t      - 278\n614\t      - 66.2%\n615\t  - title: 'Table 10: Power Analysis'\n616\t    columns:\n617\t    - n\n618\t    - Power (WR=0.65)\n619\t    - Min Detectable WR (power=0.80)\n620\t    rows:\n621\t    - - 100\n622\t      - '0.72'\n623\t      - 62.0%\n624\t    - - 300\n625\t      - '0.97'\n626\t      - 57.5%\n627\t    - - 500\n628\t      - '0.995'\n629\t      - 56.0%\n630\t  figures_description:\n631\t  - 'Appendix Figure: Forest plot 展示 5 个 n=100 blocks 的 formal win rate + 95% Wilson\n632\t    CI， 底部 diamond 标注 pooled estimate。所有 CI 互相重叠且不含 50%，视觉化效应稳定性。\n633\t\n634\t    '\n635\t  analysis: 'n500_formal_win_rate 0.662 在 [0.58, 0.70] 范围内。p<0.001 满足 p<0.01 核心假设。\n636\t    n=500 Likert 仍 borderline (p=0.082) 是 C2 的额外弹药——即使 5× sample size 都不能 让 Likert\n637\t    检测到 pairwise 在 n=100 就发现的效应。Power analysis 解释了 why： pairwise within-subject design\n638\t    的 effective sample size 远大于 Likert between-subject。\n639\t\n640\t    '\n641\t- name: Register axis (academic/conversational)\n642\t  plan_id: exp-008\n643\t  description: '第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register 改变词汇和句法\n644\t    但不改变信息内容。Full pipeline: counterfactual gen → NLI verification → dual-direction\n645\t    pairwise scoring。三个 judge × LLMBar，n=100。\n646\t\n647\t    '\n648\t  expected_results:\n649\t    register_nli_pass_rate: 0.86\n650\t    register_nli_mean: 0.893\n651\t    register_bertscore_mean: 0.839\n652\t    register_both_pass: 0.83\n653\t    gpt4o_academic_win_rate: 0.66\n654\t    gpt4o_n_consistent: 53\n655\t    gpt4o_p: 0.015\n656\t    claude_academic_win_rate: 0.62\n657\t    claude_n_consistent: 50\n658\t    claude_p: 0.042\n659\t    gemini_academic_win_rate: 0.714\n660\t    gemini_n_consistent: 56\n661\t    gemini_p: 0.003\n662\t    judges_significant: 3\n663\t    mean_academic_winrate: 0.665\n664\t    gpt4o_likert_p: 0.289\n665\t    claude_likert_p: 0.511\n666\t    gemini_likert_p: 0.167\n667\t    register_likert_pairwise_gap: true\n668\t  result_rationale: 'Register (academic vs conversational) 是 surface-level 词汇+句法变换，不改变信息内容：\n669\t    Latinate 术语 vs everyday words, 复杂从句 vs 简单句, disciplinary jargon vs lay terms。\n670\t    效应在 formality 和 tone 之间 (mean 0.665)，因为 register 涉及词汇和句法层面变化 但比 formality 更窄——formality\n671\t    包含 register + tone + 其他 cues 的 composite。 NLI pass 0.86 略低于 formality (0.88)，因为\n672\t    academic vocabulary 有时引入微妙语义偏移 (术语替代 layman terms 可能 shift specificity)。Judge\n673\t    梯度保持 Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude， 进一步确认这是 judge 内在属性而非 axis-specific 现象。所有 Likert\n674\t    p 均不显著， 扩展了 C2 blindspot evidence 到第二个 axis。\n675\t\n676\t    '\n677\t  tables:\n678\t  - title: 'Table A2: Register (Academic vs Conversational) Pairwise Results (LLMBar)'\n679\t    columns:\n680\t    - Judge\n681\t    - n_consistent\n682\t    - Academic Wins\n683\t    - Conv. Wins\n684\t    - Win Rate\n685\t    - Pairwise p\n686\t    - Likert p\n687\t    rows:\n688\t    - - GPT-4o\n689\t      - 53\n690\t      - 35\n691\t      - 18\n692\t      - 66.0%\n693\t      - 0.015*\n694\t      - '0.289'\n695\t    - - Claude-Sonnet\n696\t      - 50\n697\t      - 31\n698\t      - 19\n699\t      - 62.0%\n700\t      - 0.042*\n701\t      - '0.511'\n702\t    - - Gemini-Flash\n703\t      - 56\n704\t      - 40\n705\t      - 16\n706\t      - 71.4%\n707\t      - 0.003**\n708\t      - '0.167'\n709\t  - title: 'Table A3: Cross-Axis Summary (LLMBar, 3 judges)'\n710\t    columns:\n711\t    - Axis\n712\t    - Mean WR\n713\t    - Judges Sig. (3)\n714\t    - NLI Pass\n715\t    - Likert Detects?\n716\t    rows:\n717\t    - - Formality\n718\t      - 68.5%\n719\t      - 3/3\n720\t      - 88%\n721\t      - 0/3\n722\t    - - Register\n723\t      - 66.5%\n724\t      - 3/3\n725\t      - 86%\n726\t      - 0/3\n727\t    - - Tone\n728\t      - —\n729\t      - —\n730\t      - 65% (failed)\n731\t      - N/A\n732\t    - - Verbosity\n733\t      - —\n734\t      - —\n735\t      - 65% (failed)\n736\t      - N/A\n737\t  figures_description:\n738\t  - 'Appendix Figure: Cross-axis bar chart。四个 axes，每个三柱 (GPT-4o, Claude, Gemini)。\n739\t    Formality 和 Register 均高于 50% baseline，Tone 和 Verbosity 标注 \"Failed H1\"。 视觉化 CSD\n740\t    的 axis-dependent 有效性。\n741\t\n742\t    '\n743\t  analysis: 'Register 作为第二个 working axis 将 C3 从 \"only formality works\" 提升为 \"content-preserving\n744\t    surface-level axes generally work\"。效应量级系统性排序 formality > register > (tone/verbosity\n745\t    failed)，与 linguistic level 数量正相关： formality 跨词汇+句法+语用，register 跨词汇+句法，tone 主要在语用层。\n746\t    这提供了 principled taxonomy：改变 surface form 而不改变 information content 或 epistemic\n747\t    commitment 的 axes 适用于 CSD。\n748\t\n749\t    '\n750\t- name: Non-Qwen rewriter control\n751\t  plan_id: exp-009\n752\t  description: '使用 Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct 作为替代 rewriter，对 LLMBar formality 运行完整 pipeline。\n753\t    与 Qwen3-32B 结果比较，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。GPT-4o 作为 judge。\n754\t\n755\t    '\n756\t  expected_results:\n757\t    llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n758\t    llama_nli_mean: 0.881\n759\t    llama_bertscore_mean: 0.836\n760\t    llama_n_consistent: 52\n761\t    llama_formal_win_rate: 0.66\n762\t    llama_sign_test_p: 0.015\n763\t    qwen_nli_pass_rate: 0.88\n764\t    qwen_formal_win_rate: 0.691\n765\t    qwen_sign_test_p: 0.006\n766\t    winrate_difference: 0.031\n767\t    fisher_exact_p_for_difference: 0.42\n768\t    rewriter_effect_significant: false\n769\t  result_rationale: 'Llama rewriter 产生略低但仍显著的 formality premium (0.66 vs 0.69)，差异不显著\n770\t    (Fisher p=0.42)。NLI pass rate 略低 (0.85 vs 0.88) 因为 Llama-70B 在 instruction following\n771\t    上略弱于 Qwen3-32B (后者受益于 Qwen3 的强 instruction tuning)，导致少量 counterfactual 有轻微语义偏移。3%\n772\t    win rate 差异在统计噪声范围内，排除了 \"Qwen rewriter 引入某种被 judge 偏好的 writing pattern\" 的 confound。\n773\t    关键论点：formality bias 检测不依赖于特定 rewriter family。\n774\t\n775\t    '\n776\t  tables:\n777\t  - title: 'Table A4: Rewriter Ablation (GPT-4o × LLMBar, Formality)'\n778\t    columns:\n779\t    - Rewriter\n780\t    - NLI Pass\n781\t    - Formal WR\n782\t    - Pairwise p\n783\t    - n_consistent\n784\t    rows:\n785\t    - - Qwen3-32B\n786\t      - 88%\n787\t      - 69.1%\n788\t      - 0.006**\n789\t      - 55\n790\t    - - Llama-3.1-70B\n791\t      - 85%\n792\t      - 66.0%\n793\t      - 0.015*\n794\t      - 52\n795\t    - - Difference\n796\t      - -3%\n797\t      - -3.1%\n798\t      - Fisher p=0.42\n799\t      - —\n800\t  figures_description: []\n801\t  analysis: 'Appendix 级实验，但对 reviewer 质疑 rewriter choice 时提供决定性回应。 两个不同 family 的 rewriter\n802\t    产生一致的 formality premium，确认效应的 robustness。\n803\t\n804\t    '\n805\t- name: Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\n806\t  plan_id: exp-010\n807\t  description: 'DREAM CRITICAL。对已有 scored_32b.jsonl 数据做 sign test：每对中 formal version\n808\t    的 Likert score 是否严格高于 casual version？如果 binarized Likert sign test 也显著 → gap 是\n809\t    test choice 差异，非 measurement method 差异。如果不显著 → 确认 C2。 零成本重分析。\n810\t\n811\t    '\n812\t  expected_results:\n813\t    data_source: scored_32b.jsonl (GPT-4o × LLMBar, n=88 primary)\n814\t    n_primary: 88\n815\t    n_formal_higher: 29\n816\t    n_casual_higher: 21\n817\t    n_tied: 38\n818\t    tie_fraction: 0.432\n819\t    n_non_tied: 50\n820\t    binarized_formal_rate: 0.58\n821\t    sign_test_p: 0.24\n822\t    is_significant: false\n823\t    strict_binarize_diff_ge2:\n824\t      n_non_tied: 18\n825\t      formal_wins: 11\n826\t      sign_test_p: 0.48\n827\t    pairwise_formal_wr: 0.691\n828\t    pairwise_p: 0.006\n829\t    gap_confirmed: true\n830\t  result_rationale: 'Binarized Likert 不显著 (p=0.24) 的根因是 Likert scale 的 discretization\n831\t    loss。 在 1-10 量表上，formality 引入的 quality perception 差异约 0.10 分 (从 Likert ATE)， 这远小于一个\n832\t    scale step。因此 43.2% 的 pair 获得相同 Likert score (tied)——这些 pair 中 judge 确实感知到了 formality\n833\t    差异 (pairwise 中会做出选择)，但 Likert 的 粗粒度量表无法捕捉这个差异。在 50 个 non-tied pairs 中，formal 略占优\n834\t    (58%) 但 sample size 太小 (n=50 而非 pairwise 的 n=55 consistent)，sign test power 不足。\n835\t    即使用更严格的 binarization (score difference ≥ 2)，n 降到 18，formal 11/18 (61%) 但 p=0.48\n836\t    更加不显著。关键 insight: pairwise 的 forced-choice 消除了 tie 问题—— judge 必须在两个版本间选择，将 Likert\n837\t    中被 tie 掩盖的微弱偏好显现出来。 这证明 Likert-Pairwise gap 是 measurement granularity 差异，非 statistical\n838\t    test 选择差异。\n839\t\n840\t    '\n841\t  tables:\n842\t  - title: 'Table 11: Binarized Likert vs Pairwise — C2 Decisive Test'\n843\t    columns:\n844\t    - Method\n845\t    - n (non-tied/consistent)\n846\t    - Formal Rate\n847\t    - Sign Test p\n848\t    - Conclusion\n849\t    rows:\n850\t    - - Pairwise (position-controlled)\n851\t      - 55\n852\t      - 69.1%\n853\t      - 0.006**\n854\t      - Significant bias detected\n855\t    - - Binarized Likert (score > comparison)\n856\t      - 50\n857\t      - 58.0%\n858\t      - '0.240'\n859\t      - Not significant\n860\t    - - Binarized Likert (diff ≥ 2)\n861\t      - 18\n862\t      - 61.1%\n863\t      - '0.481'\n864\t      - Not significant\n865\t    footnote: Same underlying data (scored_32b.jsonl). Pairwise detects what binarized\n866\t      Likert misses.\n867\t  figures_description:\n868\t  - 'Figure 4 (or Figure 1 panel C): 三柱对比图。柱1: Pairwise formal rate 69.1% (显著, 深色)。\n869\t    柱2: Binarized Likert formal rate 58.0% (不显著, 浅色)。柱3: Raw Likert ATE p=0.33 (不显著,\n870\t    浅色)。标注 \"43% of Likert pairs tied — pairwise breaks ties\"。 这是 C2 的 visual proof。\n871\t\n872\t    '\n873\t  analysis: 'THIS IS THE DECISIVE EVIDENCE FOR C2。binarized_likert_sign_p = 0.24 在\n874\t    [0.12, 1.0] 范围内。 排除了 \"Likert 和 Pairwise 用不同 statistical test 所以不可比\" 的 alternative\n875\t    explanation。 现在三种分析都使用 sign test on binary outcome，唯一差异是 measurement method： (1)\n876\t    Pairwise forced-choice → 69.1%, p=0.006 (2) Binarized Likert score comparison\n877\t    → 58.0%, p=0.24 (3) Raw Likert ATE → p=0.33 Pairwise 胜出是因为它消除了 Likert 的 tie problem\n878\t    (43% tied) 和 between-item calibration noise。 Main Result Table 中增加 Binarized Likert\n879\t    列是 C2 的命门证据。\n880\t\n881\t    '\n882\t- name: NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\n883\t  plan_id: exp-011\n884\t  description: '在 70%, 75%, 80%, 85%, 90%, 95% 六个 NLI threshold 上重新计算 formality pairwise\n885\t    results。 验证结论对 threshold 选择的 robustness。零成本重分析已有 pairwise_32b 数据。\n886\t\n887\t    '\n888\t  expected_results:\n889\t    data_source: pairwise_results_32b.jsonl (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\n890\t    thresholds:\n891\t      nli_70:\n892\t        n_pairs_pass: 96\n893\t        n_consistent: 53\n894\t        formal_wins: 37\n895\t        formal_wr: 0.698\n896\t        sign_test_p: 0.005\n897\t      nli_75:\n898\t        n_pairs_pass: 94\n899\t        n_consistent: 52\n900\t        formal_wins: 36\n901\t        formal_wr: 0.692\n902\t        sign_test_p: 0.006\n903\t      nli_80:\n904\t        n_pairs_pass: 88\n905\t        n_consistent: 50\n906\t        formal_wins: 35\n907\t        formal_wr: 0.7\n908\t        sign_test_p: 0.005\n909\t      nli_85:\n910\t        n_pairs_pass: 72\n911\t        n_consistent: 42\n912\t        formal_wins: 31\n913\t        formal_wr: 0.738\n914\t        sign_test_p: 0.003\n915\t      nli_90:\n916\t        n_pairs_pass: 52\n917\t        n_consistent: 46\n918\t        formal_wins: 34\n919\t        formal_wr: 0.739\n920\t        sign_test_p: 0.002\n921\t      nli_95:\n922\t        n_pairs_pass: 36\n923\t        n_consistent: 28\n924\t        formal_wins: 21\n925\t        formal_wr: 0.75\n926\t        sign_test_p: 0.013\n927\t    all_significant_70_to_95: true\n928\t    winrate_trend: monotonically increasing (0.698 → 0.750)\n929\t    p_value_trend: decreasing then increasing (0.005 → 0.002 → 0.013) due to n tradeoff\n930\t    significant_range: 70%-95%\n931\t  result_rationale: 'Formality effect 在所有 NLI threshold 上均显著，因为 formality 改写是高质量的\n932\t    surface-level 变换——即使在宽松 threshold (70%) 下加入的额外 pairs 中有一些 semantic drift， formality\n933\t    premium 仍然 dominant。Win rate 随 threshold 提高而单调递增 (0.698→0.750)， 说明 cleaner pairs\n934\t    (higher NLI) 的 formality effect 更纯——content preservation 越好， observed bias 越接近\n935\t    true causal effect。p 值在 85-90% 处最低 (0.002)，因为此处 n (42-46) 与 effect size (0.74)\n936\t    达到最佳平衡；95% threshold 下 n 降到 28， 尽管 effect size 最高 (0.75)，power 损失导致 p 略升至 0.013，但仍远低于\n937\t    0.05。 Tone 的 NLI 在 72% 处 borderline——sensitivity analysis 显示即使在 70% threshold\n938\t    下 formality 仍稳健，这不是 threshold tuning 的结果。\n939\t\n940\t    '\n941\t  tables:\n942\t  - title: 'Table 12: NLI Threshold Sensitivity (GPT-4o × LLMBar, Formality Pairwise)'\n943\t    columns:\n944\t    - NLI Threshold\n945\t    - n_pass\n946\t    - n_consistent\n947\t    - Formal WR\n948\t    - Sign Test p\n949\t    rows:\n950\t    - - ≥70%\n951\t      - 96\n952\t      - 53\n953\t      - 69.8%\n954\t      - 0.005**\n955\t    - - ≥75%\n956\t      - 94\n957\t      - 52\n958\t      - 69.2%\n959\t      - 0.006**\n960\t    - - ≥80%\n961\t      - 88\n962\t      - 50\n963\t      - 70.0%\n964\t      - 0.005**\n965\t    - - ≥85%\n966\t      - 72\n967\t      - 42\n968\t      - 73.8%\n969\t      - 0.003**\n970\t    - - ≥90%\n971\t      - 52\n972\t      - 46\n973\t      - 73.9%\n974\t      - 0.002**\n975\t    - - ≥95%\n976\t      - 36\n977\t      - 28\n978\t      - 75.0%\n979\t      - 0.013*\n980\t    footnote: 'All thresholds from 70% to 95% yield significant results. Default threshold:\n981\t      80%.'\n982\t  figures_description:\n983\t  - 'Figure 4: 双 Y 轴折线图。X 轴: NLI threshold (70%-95%)。左 Y 轴 (蓝线): formal win rate，\n984\t    缓慢上升。右 Y 轴 (红线): -log10(p)，先升后降 (n-effect size tradeoff)。 水平虚线标注 p=0.05。所有 threshold\n985\t    点均在虚线之上。阴影区标注 \"default threshold\"。\n986\t\n987\t    '\n988\t  analysis: 'nli_threshold_sensitivity_significant_range = [''70%-95%'']，完美匹配核心假设。\n989\t    结论不依赖 threshold 选择——从最宽松 (70%) 到最严格 (95%) 均显著。 Win rate 随 threshold 上升这一 monotonic\n990\t    trend 说明 content preservation quality 与 formality effect purity 正相关，支持 CSD 的 causal\n991\t    interpretation。\n992\t\n993\t    '\n994\t- name: Consistency filter bias analysis\n995\t  plan_id: exp-012\n996\t  description: '比较 position-consistent pairs vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI scores、text\n997\t    lengths、 task types，检查 42-52% 的 discard rate 是否引入系统性偏差。零成本重分析。\n998\t\n999\t    '\n1000\t  expected_results:\n1001\t    data_source: pairwise_results_32b.jsonl\n1002\t    total_valid_pairs: 98\n1003\t    n_consistent: 55\n1004\t    n_inconsistent: 43\n1005\t    discard_rate: 0.439\n1006\t    consistent_nli_mean: 0.903\n1007\t    inconsistent_nli_mean: 0.886\n1008\t    nli_ttest_p: 0.42\n1009\t    nli_difference_significant: false\n1010\t    consistent_text_length_mean: 142.3\n1011\t    inconsistent_text_length_mean: 137.8\n1012\t    length_ttest_p: 0.58\n1013\t    length_difference_significant: false\n1014\t    consistent_formal_orig_fraction: 0.6\n1015\t    inconsistent_formal_orig_fraction: 0.558\n1016\t    orig_style_chi2_p: 0.67\n1017\t    orig_style_difference_significant: false\n1018\t    consistent_bertscore_mean: 0.848\n1019\t    inconsistent_bertscore_mean: 0.834\n1020\t    bertscore_ttest_p: 0.38\n1021\t    bertscore_difference_significant: false\n1022\t    task_type_chi2_p: 0.73\n1023\t    task_type_difference_significant: false\n1024\t    any_significant_difference: false\n1025\t    filter_introduces_bias: false\n1026\t  result_rationale: 'Position-consistency filtering 不引入系统性偏差，因为 position inconsistency\n1027\t    的主要来源 是 judge 的 confidence 而非 pair 的 systematic properties。Judge 对某些 pairs 有明确偏好\n1028\t    (无论位置如何都选同一个) → consistent，对另一些 pairs 犹豫不决 (位置影响选择) → inconsistent。 犹豫不决与 pair\n1029\t    的 NLI、text length、task type 无关，而与 quality 差异的微妙程度有关—— 当两个版本在 judge 眼中 \"差不多好\" 时，position\n1030\t    成为 tie-breaker。这是随机噪声， 不是对特定类型 pair 的系统性过滤。NLI 略高 (0.903 vs 0.886) 但 p=0.42 不显著，\n1031\t    说明 content preservation 质量不驱动 consistency。consistent pairs 中 formal-original fraction\n1032\t    (0.60) 略高于 inconsistent (0.56)，但差异远不显著 (p=0.67)，排除了 \"filtering selects for original-preference-aligned\n1033\t    pairs\" 的 confound。\n1034\t\n1035\t    '\n1036\t  tables:\n1037\t  - title: 'Table A5: Consistency Filter Bias Analysis (GPT-4o × LLMBar)'\n1038\t    columns:\n1039\t    - Property\n1040\t    - Consistent (n=55)\n1041\t    - Inconsistent (n=43)\n1042\t    - Test\n1043\t    - p\n1044\t    rows:\n1045\t    - - NLI Mean\n1046\t      - '0.903'\n1047\t      - '0.886'\n1048\t      - t-test\n1049\t      - '0.42'\n1050\t    - - Text Length (words)\n1051\t      - '142.3'\n1052\t      - '137.8'\n1053\t      - t-test\n1054\t      - '0.58'\n1055\t    - - BERTScore Mean\n1056\t      - '0.848'\n1057\t      - '0.834'\n1058\t      - t-test\n1059\t      - '0.38'\n1060\t    - - Formal-Original %\n1061\t      - 60.0%\n1062\t      - 55.8%\n1063\t      - χ²\n1064\t      - '0.67'\n1065\t    - - Task Type Distribution\n1066\t      - —\n1067\t      - —\n1068\t      - χ²\n1069\t      - '0.73'\n1070\t    footnote: No significant differences. Consistency filtering does not systematically\n1071\t      bias the retained sample.\n1072\t  figures_description: []\n1073\t  analysis: '所有 5 个 comparison 均不显著 (最小 p=0.38)，conclusively 排除 systematic filter\n1074\t    bias。 42-52% 的 discard rate 虽高，但 discarded pairs 与 retained pairs 在 observables\n1075\t    上 indistinguishable。Reviewer 对 \"high discard rate → biased sample\" 的 concern 可用此表直接回应。建议放在\n1076\t    Appendix 作为 methodological robustness check。\n1077\t\n1078\t    '\n1079\t- name: Human NLI validation (80 annotations)\n1080\t  plan_id: exp-013\n1081\t  description: 'Human validation of NLI gate decisions。对 80 个 counterfactual pairs\n1082\t    做人工标注： content 是否 preserved。报告 human-NLI agreement (Cohen''s κ)。 可使用 LLM-as-annotator\n1083\t    (GPT-4) + human spot check 的混合策略。\n1084\t\n1085\t    '\n1086\t  expected_results:\n1087\t    n_annotated: 80\n1088\t    n_nli_high: 50\n1089\t    n_nli_low: 30\n1090\t    human_preserved: 62\n1091\t    human_not_preserved: 18\n1092\t    human_preservation_rate: 0.775\n1093\t    nli_preserved: 58\n1094\t    nli_not_preserved: 22\n1095\t    both_preserved: 54\n1096\t    both_not_preserved: 14\n1097\t    nli_preserved_human_not: 4\n1098\t    nli_not_preserved_human_yes: 8\n1099\t    raw_agreement: 0.85\n1100\t    cohens_kappa: 0.72\n1101\t    kappa_interpretation: substantial agreement\n1102\t    nli_false_positive_rate: 0.069\n1103\t    nli_false_negative_rate: 0.129\n1104\t    false_positive_pattern: subtle information additions in formal rewrites that NLI\n1105\t      misses\n1106\t    false_negative_pattern: stylistic paraphrases that NLI over-penalizes as semantic\n1107\t      change\n1108\t  result_rationale: 'Cohen''s κ = 0.72 (substantial agreement) 因为 NLI 模型 (DeBERTa-large-MNLI)\n1109\t    的 training data 与 content preservation 判断高度对齐——NLI 本质上就是判断两个文本是否表达相同信息， 这与 \"counterfactual\n1110\t    是否保持 content\" 的判断完全一致。False positive rate 低 (6.9%) 说明 NLI gate 通过的 pairs 绝大多数确实\n1111\t    content-preserved——这是 CSD 结论可信度的基础。 False negative rate 较高 (12.9%) 说明 NLI 偏保守\n1112\t    (over-reject)，但这对 CSD 是安全的方向： over-rejection 意味着 retained pairs 的 content preservation\n1113\t    质量比 NLI score 建议的更高。 8 个 false negative 主要是 stylistic paraphrasing (如换用近义词或调整句子结构)\n1114\t    被 NLI 判为 non-entailment，但人工判断这些改变不影响信息内容。\n1115\t\n1116\t    '\n1117\t  tables:\n1118\t  - title: 'Table A6: Human-NLI Agreement on Content Preservation (n=80)'\n1119\t    columns:\n1120\t    - ''\n1121\t    - 'Human: Preserved'\n1122\t    - 'Human: Not Preserved'\n1123\t    - Total\n1124\t    rows:\n1125\t    - - 'NLI: Preserved (≥0.80)'\n1126\t      - 54\n1127\t      - 4\n1128\t      - 58\n1129\t    - - 'NLI: Not Preserved (<0.80)'\n1130\t      - 8\n1131\t      - 14\n1132\t      - 22\n1133\t    - - Total\n1134\t      - 62\n1135\t      - 18\n1136\t      - 80\n1137\t    footnote: Cohen's κ = 0.72 (substantial agreement). NLI FPR = 6.9%, FNR = 12.9%.\n1138\t  figures_description:\n1139\t  - 'Appendix Figure: Scatter plot，X 轴 NLI score (0-1)，Y 轴 human preservation judgment\n1140\t    (binary, jittered)。标注 threshold 垂直线在 0.80。右上象限 (both agree: preserved) 最密集，左下象限\n1141\t    (both agree: not preserved) 次之。右下 (NLI high, human not) = 4 点 标注为 false positives。展示\n1142\t    NLI score 与 human judgment 的一致性。\n1143\t\n1144\t    '\n1145\t  analysis: 'κ = 0.72 在 [0.61, 0.80] \"substantial\" 范围内，满足审稿人对 NLI gate 可信度的要求。 NLI\n1146\t    偏保守 (FNR > FPR) 对 CSD 有利：retained pairs 的 content preservation 质量 被 underestimate\n1147\t    而非 overestimate。建议论文中强调：\"NLI false positives are rare (6.9%), meaning pairs that\n1148\t    pass the gate genuinely preserve content.\"\n1149\t\n1150\t    '\n1151\t- name: Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\n1152\t  plan_id: exp-014\n1153\t  description: 'Logistic regression 正式分离 formality 和 original preference。 Pool exp-001/002\n1154\t    所有 judge×benchmark pairwise 数据。DV: formal_preferred (1/0)。 IV: is_formal_original\n1155\t    (1/0), judge (fixed effects), benchmark (fixed effects)。 Test formality 主效应 (intercept)\n1156\t    是否显著，interaction 是否不显著。\n1157\t\n1158\t    '\n1159\t  expected_results:\n1160\t    data_source: pooled pairwise from all judge × benchmark combinations\n1161\t    n_observations: 459\n1162\t    intercept_beta: 0.52\n1163\t    intercept_se: 0.19\n1164\t    intercept_z: 2.74\n1165\t    intercept_p: 0.006\n1166\t    intercept_odds_ratio: 1.68\n1167\t    intercept_interpretation: formal 被偏好的 odds 是 casual 的 1.68 倍，controlling for original\n1168\t      status\n1169\t    is_formal_original_beta: 0.34\n1170\t    is_formal_original_se: 0.17\n1171\t    is_formal_original_z: 2.0\n1172\t    is_formal_original_p: 0.046\n1173\t    is_formal_original_or: 1.4\n1174\t    interaction_beta: 0.12\n1175\t    interaction_se: 0.22\n1176\t    interaction_z: 0.55\n1177\t    interaction_p: 0.58\n1178\t    interaction_significant: false\n1179\t    judge_claude_beta: -0.28\n1180\t    judge_claude_p: 0.11\n1181\t    judge_gemini_beta: 0.19\n1182\t    judge_gemini_p: 0.24\n1183\t    benchmark_alpacaeval_beta: -0.08\n1184\t    benchmark_alpacaeval_p: 0.62\n1185\t    benchmark_mtbench_beta: -0.15\n1186\t    benchmark_mtbench_p: 0.38\n1187\t    mcfadden_r2: 0.042\n1188\t    aic: 582.3\n1189\t    bic: 611.7\n1190\t    raw_mean_formal_wr: 0.664\n1191\t    original_preference_contribution: 0.033\n1192\t    csd_adjusted_formal_wr: 0.631\n1193\t    logistic_formality_coef_p: 0.006\n1194\t  result_rationale: 'Formality 主效应 (intercept β₀=0.52, p=0.006) 显著，说明控制 original status\n1195\t    后 formal 仍被系统性偏好——这是 formality bias 作为 independent causal effect 的统计证据。 is_formal_original\n1196\t    (β₁=0.34, p=0.046) 边缘显著，说明 original preference 确实存在 但效应量 (OR=1.40) 远小于 formality\n1197\t    (OR=1.68)。关键：interaction term 不显著 (p=0.58)， 意味着 formality 的效应不依赖于 formal 版本是否为\n1198\t    original——无论 formal 是原文还是改写， judge 都偏好它。这彻底回应了 \"observed formality bias 只是 original\n1199\t    preference 的 proxy\" 的 alternative explanation。Judge 和 benchmark fixed effects\n1200\t    不显著，说明 formality premium 在不同 judge 和 benchmark 间是 stable 的 (尽管 magnitude 有差异，\n1201\t    但 direction 一致)。CSD-adjusted formal win rate = 63.1% (扣除 original preference 贡献\n1202\t    3.3 个百分点)，这是对 reviewer 最保守友好的 headline number。\n1203\t\n1204\t    '\n1205\t  tables:\n1206\t  - title: 'Table 13: Logistic Regression — Formality vs Original Preference Decomposition'\n1207\t    columns:\n1208\t    - Predictor\n1209\t    - β\n1210\t    - SE\n1211\t    - z\n1212\t    - p\n1213\t    - Odds Ratio\n1214\t    rows:\n1215\t    - - Intercept (formality effect)\n1216\t      - '0.52'\n1217\t      - '0.19'\n1218\t      - '2.74'\n1219\t      - 0.006**\n1220\t      - '1.68'\n1221\t    - - is_formal_original\n1222\t      - '0.34'\n1223\t      - '0.17'\n1224\t      - '2.00'\n1225\t      - 0.046*\n1226\t      - '1.40'\n1227\t    - - Interaction\n1228\t      - '0.12'\n1229\t      - '0.22'\n1230\t      - '0.55'\n1231\t      - '0.583'\n1232\t      - '1.13'\n1233\t    - - 'Judge: Claude (vs GPT-4o)'\n1234\t      - '-0.28'\n1235\t      - '0.17'\n1236\t      - '-1.65'\n1237\t      - '0.110'\n1238\t      - '0.76'\n1239\t    - - 'Judge: Gemini (vs GPT-4o)'\n1240\t      - '0.19'\n1241\t      - '0.16'\n1242\t      - '1.19'\n1243\t      - '0.240'\n1244\t      - '1.21'\n1245\t    - - 'Bench: AlpacaEval (vs LLMBar)'\n1246\t      - '-0.08'\n1247\t      - '0.16'\n1248\t      - '-0.50'\n1249\t      - '0.620'\n1250\t      - '0.92'\n1251\t    - - 'Bench: MT-Bench (vs LLMBar)'\n1252\t      - '-0.15'\n1253\t      - '0.17'\n1254\t      - '-0.88'\n1255\t      - '0.380'\n1256\t      - '0.86'\n1257\t    footnote: N=459 observations pooled across 9 judge×benchmark combinations. McFadden\n1258\t      R²=0.042.\n1259\t  - title: 'Table 14: CSD-Adjusted Win Rate'\n1260\t    columns:\n1261\t    - Metric\n1262\t    - Value\n1263\t    - Source\n1264\t    rows:\n1265\t    - - Raw formal win rate (mean across combos)\n1266\t      - 66.4%\n1267\t      - exp-001/002\n1268\t    - - Original preference contribution\n1269\t      - +3.3%\n1270\t      - exp-014 β₁\n1271\t    - - CSD-adjusted formal win rate\n1272\t      - 63.1%\n1273\t      - Raw − original contribution\n1274\t    - - 95% CI of adjusted rate\n1275\t      - '[57.2%, 69.0%]'\n1276\t      - Bootstrap\n1277\t  figures_description:\n1278\t  - 'Figure 5 (main): Effect decomposition waterfall chart。 Bar 1: Raw formal WR =\n1279\t    66.4%。 Bar 2: −3.3% (original preference, green downward)。 Bar 3: Net formality\n1280\t    causal effect = 63.1% (blue, 13.1% above 50% baseline)。 Error bars on final bar\n1281\t    from bootstrap CI。 Visual proof that formality effect survives original preference\n1282\t    correction。\n1283\t\n1284\t    '\n1285\t  analysis: logistic_formality_coef_p = 0.006 在 [0.001, 0.05] 范围内。Interaction p =\n1286\t    0.58 明确不显著。C4 (practical guidance) 有了统计基础：CSD-adjusted win rate 公式为 adjusted_wr\n1287\t    = raw_wr - β₁/(β₀+β₁) × (raw_wr - 0.50)。这比 ad-hoc additive correction 更有统计根据。Paper\n1288\t    可以给出 practitioner checklist：(1) use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit;\n1289\t    (2) run RATE control to quantify original preference; (3) report both raw and\n1290\t    CSD-adjusted win rates; (4) verify content preservation per axis before applying\n1291\t    CSD。\n1292\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6e97501-db33-49e4-82d6-a111de115694","uuid":"b53ba418-098e-4632-9ec0-9b3bced71ffb","timestamp":"2026-05-21T00:18:16.699Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T233719/best/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '原始 \"Likert Blindspot\" framing 完全成立。 C2 是 primary contribution：exp-010\n  binarized Likert sign test 不显著 (p=0.24)，确认 gap 是 measurement 结构差异而非统计检验选择差异。3 个\n  judge × 3 个 benchmark 中 7/9 组合出现 Likert-Pairwise gap， 无 reverse pattern。C1 作为 application\n  contribution 诚实定位，组件来源全部 acknowledge。 C3 降级为 preliminary：formality robust + register\n  作为第二 working axis + tone/verbosity 作为 principled boundary。C4 通过 logistic regression\n  (exp-014) formality 主效应独立显著 (p=0.006) 提供 CSD-adjusted win rate 的统计基础。n=500 复制 (exp-006)\n  消除 sample size 质疑。 NLI threshold sensitivity (exp-011) 证明结果在 70%-95% 范围内 robust。\n  Human validation (exp-013) κ=0.72 证明 NLI gate 不是 black box。 Headline: \"Standard\n  Likert scoring misses style bias that pairwise comparison detects across 3 judges\n  and 3 benchmarks — a structural measurement limitation, not a statistical artifact,\n  confirmed by binarized Likert control.\" Main result table 中 binarized Likert 列提供\n  C2 决定性证据。 25+ refs 到位，projected review score 4.0-4.5，直冲 Main。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Multi-judge formality pairwise\n  plan_id: exp-001\n  description: '在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 formality pairwise 实验。\n    使用已生成的 counterfactual pairs (n=100)，每个 judge 做 dual-direction pairwise， position\n    control。与 GPT-4o baseline (69.1%, p=0.006) 对比。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.691\n    gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.006\n    gpt4o_n_consistent: 55\n    gpt4o_formal_wins: 38\n    gpt4o_casual_wins: 17\n    claude_sonnet_formal_win_rate: 0.64\n    claude_sonnet_sign_test_p: 0.028\n    claude_sonnet_n_consistent: 50\n    claude_sonnet_formal_wins: 32\n    claude_sonnet_casual_wins: 18\n    claude_sonnet_consistency_rate: 0.51\n    gemini_flash_formal_win_rate: 0.724\n    gemini_flash_sign_test_p: 0.002\n    gemini_flash_n_consistent: 58\n    gemini_flash_formal_wins: 42\n    gemini_flash_casual_wins: 16\n    gemini_flash_consistency_rate: 0.59\n    n_judges_significant_after_holm: 3\n    holm_corrected_p_values:\n      gemini: 0.006\n      gpt4o: 0.012\n      claude: 0.028\n    cross_judge_mean_winrate: 0.685\n    cross_judge_winrate_range:\n    - 0.64\n    - 0.724\n    cross_judge_pairwise_p_median: 0.006\n  result_rationale: 'Formality bias 是 LLM judge 的通用现象而非 GPT-4o 特有。三个 judge 的 RLHF\n    训练数据 普遍偏向 formal/professional 风格回答，formal text 与 higher-quality content 在 pretraining\n    语料中高度相关。Claude-Sonnet 效应略弱 (0.64) 因为 Anthropic 的 RLHF 有更多 helpfulness 导向校准，对 surface\n    style 依赖稍低；Gemini-Flash 效应略强 (0.72) 因为轻量模型更依赖 surface heuristics 作为 quality proxy。三者量级差异\n    (0.64-0.72) 本身也是 C3 evidence—— bias magnitude 是 judge-dependent 的。Holm correction\n    后全部 p<0.05，因为每个 judge 的 raw p 都足够小 (最大 0.028)，3 重比较惩罚不足以翻转。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 2: Formality Pairwise Results Across Judges (LLMBar, n=100)'\n    columns:\n    - Judge\n    - n_consistent\n    - Formal Wins\n    - Casual Wins\n    - Win Rate\n    - 95% CI\n    - Sign Test p\n    - Holm p\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - 55\n      - 38\n      - 17\n      - 69.1%\n      - '[56.0%, 79.7%]'\n      - 0.006**\n      - 0.012*\n    - - Claude-Sonnet\n      - 50\n      - 32\n      - 18\n      - 64.0%\n      - '[50.1%, 75.9%]'\n      - 0.028*\n      - 0.028*\n    - - Gemini-Flash\n      - 58\n      - 42\n      - 16\n      - 72.4%\n      - '[59.8%, 82.3%]'\n      - 0.002**\n      - 0.006**\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 3 (partial): 3×3 heatmap 的 LLMBar 列。色阶从 50% (neutral) 到 75% (strong bias)，\n    三个 judge 均深色，视觉化 cross-judge 一致性。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'A1 假设成立：3/3 judge 在 Holm correction 后显著。cross_judge_mean_winrate 0.685\n    在 [0.60, 0.75] 范围中上。Judge 间量级差异 (Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude) 稳定， 为 C3 axis-dependency\n    提供 judge 维度证据。Direction asymmetry 在所有 judge 上存在 (formal-original 方向更强)，为 exp-005\n    original preference 控制提供动机。\n\n    '\n- name: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\n  plan_id: exp-002\n  description: '在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上运行 CSD 流程。新 counterfactual generation (不同\n    source text)。 三个 judge (GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash) 分别评测。每个 benchmark\n    n=100。 与 LLMBar 结果交叉比较，形成 3×3 矩阵。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.67\n    alpacaeval_gpt4o_p: 0.012\n    alpacaeval_claude_formal_winrate: 0.61\n    alpacaeval_claude_p: 0.048\n    alpacaeval_gemini_formal_winrate: 0.7\n    alpacaeval_gemini_p: 0.004\n    alpacaeval_counterfactual_nli_pass: 0.9\n    alpacaeval_nli_mean: 0.908\n    mtbench_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.65\n    mtbench_gpt4o_p: 0.018\n    mtbench_claude_formal_winrate: 0.6\n    mtbench_claude_p: 0.065\n    mtbench_gemini_formal_winrate: 0.68\n    mtbench_gemini_p: 0.008\n    mtbench_counterfactual_nli_pass: 0.87\n    mtbench_nli_mean: 0.882\n    n_benchmarks_with_gap: 3\n    significant_combos_total: 7\n    total_combos: 9\n    non_significant_combos:\n    - Claude×MT-Bench (p=0.065, borderline)\n    borderline_combos: 1\n    mean_winrate_across_all_9: 0.664\n  result_rationale: 'Formality bias 跨 benchmark 泛化，因为 bias 源于 judge 内在偏好而非特定数据集特征。\n    AlpacaEval 效应略强于 MT-Bench：open-ended instruction-following 任务给 style variation\n    更大空间，formal tone 作为 quality proxy 权重更大；MT-Bench 的 multi-turn 结构和更 specific 的评判标准\n    (如 math/reasoning accuracy) 部分抑制了 style 影响。Claude×MT-Bench 是唯一 borderline 不显著的组合\n    (p=0.065)，因为 Claude 在有明确正确性标准的 benchmark 上更倾向 content-based 判断，且 Claude 本身 formality\n    sensitivity 最低。NLI pass rate 在 AlpacaEval (0.90) 略高于 MT-Bench (0.87)，因为 AlpacaEval\n    response 结构更简单， counterfactual 改写更容易保持语义。7/9 显著远超偶然水平。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 3: Formality Pairwise Win Rate Matrix (Judge × Benchmark)'\n    columns:\n    - Judge\n    - LLMBar\n    - AlpacaEval\n    - MT-Bench\n    - Mean\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - 69.1%**\n      - 67.0%*\n      - 65.0%*\n      - 67.0%\n    - - Claude-Sonnet\n      - 64.0%*\n      - 61.0%*\n      - 60.0%†\n      - 61.7%\n    - - Gemini-Flash\n      - 72.4%**\n      - 70.0%**\n      - 68.0%**\n      - 70.1%\n    - - Mean\n      - 68.5%\n      - 66.0%\n      - 64.3%\n      - 66.3%\n    footnote: '** p<0.01, * p<0.05, † p<0.10. n=100 per cell, n_consistent varies\n      48-58.'\n  - title: 'Table 4: Counterfactual Quality per Benchmark'\n    columns:\n    - Benchmark\n    - n\n    - NLI Pass Rate\n    - NLI Mean\n    - BERTScore Mean\n    rows:\n    - - LLMBar\n      - 100\n      - 88%\n      - 0.896\n      - 0.842\n    - - AlpacaEval\n      - 100\n      - 90%\n      - 0.908\n      - 0.851\n    - - MT-Bench\n      - 100\n      - 87%\n      - 0.882\n      - 0.835\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 3 (main): 3 judges × 3 benchmarks heatmap，cell 内标注 win rate 和显著性星号。 色阶：50%=白色,\n    60%=浅蓝, 70%=深蓝, 80%=深色。视觉传达 cross-judge × cross-benchmark 一致的 formality premium。唯一浅色\n    cell 是 Claude×MT-Bench (60.0%†)。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'A2 假设成立：3/3 benchmarks 显示 gap。Benchmark 梯度 (LLMBar > AlpacaEval > MT-Bench)\n    有方法论意义——task-specific evaluation criteria 越强，style bias 越被抑制。 Judge 梯度 (Gemini\n    > GPT-4o > Claude) 稳定跨 benchmark，说明 judge 的 style sensitivity 是其内在属性而非 benchmark\n    artifact。9 个组合的 mean win rate 0.664 在 cross_judge_formal_win_rate [0.60, 0.75]\n    范围内。\n\n    '\n- name: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\n  plan_id: exp-003\n  description: '对 exp-001/002 的每个 judge×benchmark 组合，计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win\n    rate， 系统性比较两种 measurement 的 sensitivity。同一 counterfactual 数据。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    llmbar_gpt4o_likert_ate: 0.1\n    llmbar_gpt4o_likert_p: 0.332\n    llmbar_gpt4o_pairwise_p: 0.006\n    llmbar_claude_likert_ate: 0.06\n    llmbar_claude_likert_p: 0.485\n    llmbar_claude_pairwise_p: 0.028\n    llmbar_gemini_likert_ate: 0.14\n    llmbar_gemini_likert_p: 0.198\n    llmbar_gemini_pairwise_p: 0.002\n    alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_ate: 0.08\n    alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_p: 0.412\n    alpacaeval_claude_likert_ate: 0.04\n    alpacaeval_claude_likert_p: 0.551\n    alpacaeval_gemini_likert_ate: 0.12\n    alpacaeval_gemini_likert_p: 0.142\n    mtbench_gpt4o_likert_ate: 0.09\n    mtbench_gpt4o_likert_p: 0.388\n    mtbench_claude_likert_ate: 0.03\n    mtbench_claude_likert_p: 0.612\n    mtbench_gemini_likert_ate: 0.11\n    mtbench_gemini_likert_p: 0.175\n    combos_with_gap: 7\n    combos_without_gap: 2\n    combos_total: 9\n    gap_note: 2 个无 gap：Claude×MT-Bench (两者都不显著，一致性 non-sig)，Gemini×AlpacaEval Likert\n      p=0.142 borderline\n    median_likert_p: 0.388\n    median_pairwise_p: 0.012\n    cross_judge_likert_ate_p_median: 0.37\n    no_reverse_pattern: true\n  result_rationale: 'Likert-Pairwise gap 的根因是 measurement scale 的信息结构差异。Likert pointwise\n    评分中， style bias 被三个机制稀释：(1) score anchoring——judge 倾向使用量表中段，微小 style 偏好 不足以跨越\n    score boundary；(2) absolute calibration noise——不同 item 的 baseline quality 差异远大于\n    style 引入的差异，between-item variance 淹没 within-item style effect； (3) 离散量表的 resolution\n    limit——1-10 scale 上 0.10 的 ATE 被四舍五入吸收。 Pairwise 直接呈现 A/B 对比，消除 absolute calibration\n    问题，将 style 差异放大为 forced choice 中的 tie-breaking signal。Gemini 的 Likert p (0.142-0.198)\n    最接近显著， 因为 Gemini 的 formality premium 最强 (72.4%)，即使 Likert 的稀释也无法完全消除。 但仍未达 p<0.05，确认\n    Likert blindspot 的系统性。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 5: Likert ATE vs Pairwise Win Rate — The Likert Blindspot'\n    columns:\n    - Judge × Benchmark\n    - Likert ATE\n    - Likert p\n    - Pairwise WR\n    - Pairwise p\n    - Gap?\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-4o × LLMBar\n      - '+0.10'\n      - '0.332'\n      - 69.1%\n      - 0.006**\n      - ✓\n    - - Claude × LLMBar\n      - '+0.06'\n      - '0.485'\n      - 64.0%\n      - 0.028*\n      - ✓\n    - - Gemini × LLMBar\n      - '+0.14'\n      - '0.198'\n      - 72.4%\n      - 0.002**\n      - ✓\n    - - GPT-4o × AlpacaEval\n      - '+0.08'\n      - '0.412'\n      - 67.0%\n      - 0.012*\n      - ✓\n    - - Claude × AlpacaEval\n      - '+0.04'\n      - '0.551'\n      - 61.0%\n      - 0.048*\n      - ✓\n    - - Gemini × AlpacaEval\n      - '+0.12'\n      - '0.142'\n      - 70.0%\n      - 0.004**\n      - ✓\n    - - GPT-4o × MT-Bench\n      - '+0.09'\n      - '0.388'\n      - 65.0%\n      - 0.018*\n      - ✓\n    - - Claude × MT-Bench\n      - '+0.03'\n      - '0.612'\n      - 60.0%\n      - 0.065†\n      - —\n    - - Gemini × MT-Bench\n      - '+0.11'\n      - '0.175'\n      - 68.0%\n      - 0.008**\n      - ✓\n    footnote: Gap = Likert p>0.10 AND Pairwise p<0.05. 7/9 combos show gap. 0/9 reverse\n      pattern.\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 1 (main, problem illustration): 双面板对比图。左: Likert ATE 带 95% CI error bar，\n    所有 9 个组合 CI 均跨零线。右: Pairwise win rate 带 Wilson CI，7/9 CI 不含 50%。 视觉冲击力：同一数据、两种\n    measurement、截然不同的结论。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'C2 的核心 evidence。7/9 组合出现系统性 measurement gap，且无 reverse pattern (没有任何组合\n    Likert 显著但 Pairwise 不显著)。median Likert p = 0.37 在 [0.15, 0.5] 范围内， median Pairwise\n    p = 0.012 在 [0.001, 0.02] 范围内。gap 不依赖特定 judge 或 benchmark—— 这意味着现有文献中基于 Likert\n    的 style bias 研究可能系统性低估问题严重程度。 Practical implication: style bias audit 应使用 pairwise\n    comparison 而非 pointwise scoring。\n\n    '\n- name: Tone axis (assertive/hedging) — negative control\n  plan_id: exp-004\n  description: 'D014 Tone pilot 已失败 (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%)。Epistemic commitment\n    change 与 NLI verification 结构性不兼容。本实验以 pilot 数据 (n=20) 为基础，正式文档化失败模式， 作为 C3 的 axis\n    boundary evidence。不需额外 API 调用。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_pilot: 20\n    nli_cf_pass_rate: 0.65\n    nli_cf_mean: 0.704\n    bertscore_cf_mean: 0.92\n    joint_pass_rate: 0.45\n    by_tone_assertive_both_pass: 0.385\n    by_tone_hedging_both_pass: 0.571\n    catastrophic_nli_lt001_count: 6\n    catastrophic_fraction: 0.3\n    failure_mode: assertive→hedging 改变 epistemic commitment (confidence markers, modal\n      verbs)，NLI 正确检测为 non-entailment\n    structural_incompatibility: true\n    pipeline_stopped_at: content_verification\n  result_rationale: 'Tone 改变 (assertive↔hedging) 不是纯 style 变换——它改变了说话者对命题的认知承诺程度。\n    \"X is the best approach\" vs \"X might be a reasonable approach\" 在 NLI 框架下不构成双向蕴含，\n    因为前者的 truth conditions 严格强于后者。30% 的样本出现 catastrophic NLI<0.01， 说明这不是 threshold\n    选择问题而是根本性的语义兼容性问题。Hedging 方向 (assertive→hedging) both_pass 更高 (57.1% vs 38.5%)，因为弱化断言仍蕴含弱化后的命题，但强化断言\n    (hedging→assertive) 引入了原文未承诺的确定性。这个不对称性本身就是 principled boundary 的证据：NLI gate 不是\n    arbitrary obstacle，而是正确识别了语义改变。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table A1: Tone Axis Content Verification Failure (n=20 pilot)'\n    columns:\n    - Direction\n    - n\n    - NLI Mean\n    - Both Pass Rate\n    - Catastrophic NLI<0.01\n    rows:\n    - - Assertive→Hedging\n      - 13\n      - '0.656'\n      - 38.5%\n      - 4/13 (30.8%)\n    - - Hedging→Assertive\n      - 7\n      - '0.793'\n      - 57.1%\n      - 2/7 (28.6%)\n    - - Overall\n      - 20\n      - '0.704'\n      - 45.0%\n      - 6/20 (30.0%)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Appendix Figure: NLI score distribution histogram for tone vs formality counterfactuals。\n    Formality: 右偏，集中在 0.85-1.0。Tone: 双峰分布，一峰在 0.8-1.0 (成功保留)， 一峰在 0.0-0.1 (catastrophic\n    failure)。视觉化结构性不兼容。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Tone 作为 negative control 为 C3 提供 principled method boundary：CSD 适用于 不改变认知承诺的\n    surface-level style axes (formality ✓)，不适用于改变 epistemic commitment 的 axes (tone\n    ✗)。NLI gate 在此处正确拒绝—— 这不是方法失败，而是正确的质量控制行为。Paper 中定位为 \"method boundary\" 而非 \"negative\n    result\"，因为它回答了 \"CSD 适用范围\" 这个审稿人一定会问的问题。\n\n    '\n- name: Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: 'Original text vs 同风格 double-rewrite 的 pairwise 比较，量化 original preference\n    confound。 D015: 扩展到所有 judge × LLMBar 组合。同时分析 casual-original subset (main pairwise\n    中原文为 casual 的子集) 在不同 judge 上的 formal win rate。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gpt4o_n_valid: 95\n    gpt4o_n_consistent: 60\n    gpt4o_original_wins: 32\n    gpt4o_rewrite_wins: 28\n    gpt4o_original_win_rate: 0.533\n    gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.362\n    gpt4o_wilson_ci:\n    - 0.408\n    - 0.655\n    claude_n_consistent: 55\n    claude_original_wins: 28\n    claude_rewrite_wins: 27\n    claude_original_win_rate: 0.509\n    claude_sign_test_p: 0.92\n    gemini_n_consistent: 62\n    gemini_original_wins: 34\n    gemini_rewrite_wins: 28\n    gemini_original_win_rate: 0.548\n    gemini_sign_test_p: 0.28\n    mean_original_win_rate: 0.53\n    any_judge_original_pref_significant: false\n    casual_orig_gpt4o_formal_wr: 0.545\n    casual_orig_gpt4o_p: 0.832\n    casual_orig_gpt4o_n: 22\n    casual_orig_claude_formal_wr: 0.63\n    casual_orig_claude_p: 0.072\n    casual_orig_claude_n: 27\n    casual_orig_gemini_formal_wr: 0.611\n    casual_orig_gemini_p: 0.096\n    casual_orig_gemini_n: 36\n    casual_orig_best_judge: Claude\n    casual_orig_best_judge_wr: 0.63\n    casual_orig_best_judge_p: 0.072\n  result_rationale: 'Original preference 在所有 judge 上均弱且不显著 (mean 53.0%)，因为 double-rewrite\n    过程 虽引入轻微 rewrite artifact (如稍微不自然的措辞)，但这个 artifact 对 judge 影响是随机的 而非系统性的。Claude\n    的 original preference 最弱 (50.9%)，可能因为 Claude 对 \"naturalness\" 的敏感度更低。Gemini 稍高\n    (54.8%)，可能因为轻量模型对 fluency 微妙差异更敏感。 Casual-original subset 分析是关键：Claude 上 63.0%\n    formal win rate (p=0.072) 说明即使 formality preference 与 original preference 方向相反\n    (formal = rewrite)， formality 仍占上风。这在 GPT-4o 上不显著 (54.5%) 可能因为 GPT-4o 的 original\n    preference (53.3%) 与 formality preference 恰好在 casual-original subset 上互相抵消。 Claude\n    original preference 更弱 (50.9%)，所以 formality 更容易 dominate。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 6: Original Preference Control Across Judges (LLMBar)'\n    columns:\n    - Judge\n    - n_consistent\n    - Original Wins\n    - Rewrite Wins\n    - Original WR\n    - p\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - 60\n      - 32\n      - 28\n      - 53.3%\n      - '0.362'\n    - - Claude-Sonnet\n      - 55\n      - 28\n      - 27\n      - 50.9%\n      - '0.920'\n    - - Gemini-Flash\n      - 62\n      - 34\n      - 28\n      - 54.8%\n      - '0.280'\n  - title: 'Table 7: Casual-Original Subset — Formal Win Rate When Opposing Original\n      Preference'\n    columns:\n    - Judge\n    - n_consistent\n    - Formal Wins\n    - Formal WR\n    - p\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - 22\n      - 12\n      - 54.5%\n      - '0.832'\n    - - Claude-Sonnet\n      - 27\n      - 17\n      - 63.0%\n      - 0.072†\n    - - Gemini-Flash\n      - 36\n      - 22\n      - 61.1%\n      - 0.096†\n    footnote: † p<0.10. Formal = rewrite in this subset, so original preference opposes\n      formality.\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 5 (partial): Effect decomposition bar chart。三组柱状图 (GPT-4o, Claude, Gemini)，\n    每组两柱：total formal WR (tall, ~65-72%) vs original preference WR (short, ~51-55%)。\n    差值区间标注 \"formality-attributable effect\"。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'A6 假设成立：original preference 贡献 <5 个百分点 (mean 53% - 50% = 3%)， 远小于 formality\n    premium (mean 68.5% - 50% = 18.5%)。Casual-original subset 在 Claude (63%) 和 Gemini\n    (61.1%) 上均 >60%，best judge p=0.072 满足 p<0.10。 casual_orig_best_judge_wr 0.63 在\n    [0.60, 0.70] 范围内。 Direction asymmetry (MVP 中 formal-orig 78.8% vs casual-orig\n    54.5%) 主要解释 从 \"original preference\" 转向 \"改写方向的非对称难度\"。\n\n    '\n- name: Scaled replication (n=500)\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: '将 formality pairwise 实验从 n=100 扩大到 n=500。选择效应最强的 judge×benchmark 组合\n    (Gemini×LLMBar)。Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。 五个 n=100 子组的稳定性分析。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_total: 500\n    n_valid_both_trials: 490\n    n_consistent: 278\n    consistency_rate: 0.567\n    formal_wins: 184\n    casual_wins: 94\n    formal_win_rate: 0.662\n    wilson_ci:\n    - 0.604\n    - 0.716\n    sign_test_p: 1.0e-05\n    cohens_h: 0.337\n    likert_ate_n500: 0.11\n    likert_ate_p_n500: 0.082\n    likert_still_borderline: true\n    sub1_winrate: 0.7\n    sub2_winrate: 0.65\n    sub3_winrate: 0.68\n    sub4_winrate: 0.64\n    sub5_winrate: 0.64\n    subgroup_sd: 0.026\n    power_n100_d065: 0.72\n    power_n300_d065: 0.97\n    power_n500_d065: 0.995\n    min_detectable_wr_n500: 0.56\n    nli_ge90_n_consistent: 232\n    nli_ge90_winrate: 0.685\n    nli_ge80_n_consistent: 262\n    nli_ge80_winrate: 0.668\n  result_rationale: 'n=500 时 win rate 0.662 相比 n=100 pilot 的 0.691 有 2.9% 的 regression\n    to mean， 这在预期范围内——pilot 的 point estimate 在 CI [0.56, 0.80] 上端，larger sample 收敛到\n    true effect。CI 从 [0.56, 0.80] 收窄到 [0.60, 0.72]，p 从 0.006 降到 <0.001。 五个 n=100 子组\n    win rate 在 0.64-0.70 范围波动 (σ=0.026)，展示效应高度稳定。 关键发现：即使 n=500，Likert ATE 仍仅 borderline\n    显著 (p=0.082)——这强化了 C2： Likert blindspot 不是 power 问题，而是 measurement sensitivity\n    的结构性差异。 如果仅仅是 power 问题，n=500 的 Likert 应当显著；它仍不显著说明 Likert 对 style bias 的检测本身就是\n    structurally impaired。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 8: Scaled Replication (Gemini × LLMBar, Formality)'\n    columns:\n    - Scale\n    - n_consistent\n    - Formal WR\n    - 95% CI\n    - Pairwise p\n    - Likert p\n    rows:\n    - - n=100 (MVP pilot)\n      - 55\n      - 69.1%\n      - '[56.0%, 79.7%]'\n      - 0.006**\n      - '0.332'\n    - - n=500 (replication)\n      - 278\n      - 66.2%\n      - '[60.4%, 71.6%]'\n      - <0.001***\n      - 0.082†\n    footnote: Likert p still non-significant at n=500 (borderline), confirming structural\n      measurement gap.\n  - title: 'Table 9: Subgroup Stability (5 × n=100 splits)'\n    columns:\n    - Split\n    - n_consistent\n    - Formal WR\n    rows:\n    - - Block 1\n      - 57\n      - 70.0%\n    - - Block 2\n      - 53\n      - 65.0%\n    - - Block 3\n      - 56\n      - 68.0%\n    - - Block 4\n      - 54\n      - 64.0%\n    - - Block 5\n      - 58\n      - 64.0%\n    - - Full n=500\n      - 278\n      - 66.2%\n  - title: 'Table 10: Power Analysis'\n    columns:\n    - n\n    - Power (WR=0.65)\n    - Min Detectable WR (power=0.80)\n    rows:\n    - - 100\n      - '0.72'\n      - 62.0%\n    - - 300\n      - '0.97'\n      - 57.5%\n    - - 500\n      - '0.995'\n      - 56.0%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Appendix Figure: Forest plot 展示 5 个 n=100 blocks 的 formal win rate + 95% Wilson\n    CI， 底部 diamond 标注 pooled estimate。所有 CI 互相重叠且不含 50%，视觉化效应稳定性。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'n500_formal_win_rate 0.662 在 [0.58, 0.70] 范围内。p<0.001 满足 p<0.01 核心假设。\n    n=500 Likert 仍 borderline (p=0.082) 是 C2 的额外弹药——即使 5× sample size 都不能 让 Likert\n    检测到 pairwise 在 n=100 就发现的效应。Power analysis 解释了 why： pairwise within-subject design\n    的 effective sample size 远大于 Likert between-subject。\n\n    '\n- name: Register axis (academic/conversational)\n  plan_id: exp-008\n  description: '第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register 改变词汇和句法\n    但不改变信息内容。Full pipeline: counterfactual gen → NLI verification → dual-direction\n    pairwise scoring。三个 judge × LLMBar，n=100。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    register_nli_pass_rate: 0.86\n    register_nli_mean: 0.893\n    register_bertscore_mean: 0.839\n    register_both_pass: 0.83\n    gpt4o_academic_win_rate: 0.66\n    gpt4o_n_consistent: 53\n    gpt4o_p: 0.015\n    claude_academic_win_rate: 0.62\n    claude_n_consistent: 50\n    claude_p: 0.042\n    gemini_academic_win_rate: 0.714\n    gemini_n_consistent: 56\n    gemini_p: 0.003\n    judges_significant: 3\n    mean_academic_winrate: 0.665\n    gpt4o_likert_p: 0.289\n    claude_likert_p: 0.511\n    gemini_likert_p: 0.167\n    register_likert_pairwise_gap: true\n  result_rationale: 'Register (academic vs conversational) 是 surface-level 词汇+句法变换，不改变信息内容：\n    Latinate 术语 vs everyday words, 复杂从句 vs 简单句, disciplinary jargon vs lay terms。\n    效应在 formality 和 tone 之间 (mean 0.665)，因为 register 涉及词汇和句法层面变化 但比 formality 更窄——formality\n    包含 register + tone + 其他 cues 的 composite。 NLI pass 0.86 略低于 formality (0.88)，因为\n    academic vocabulary 有时引入微妙语义偏移 (术语替代 layman terms 可能 shift specificity)。Judge\n    梯度保持 Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude， 进一步确认这是 judge 内在属性而非 axis-specific 现象。所有 Likert\n    p 均不显著， 扩展了 C2 blindspot evidence 到第二个 axis。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table A2: Register (Academic vs Conversational) Pairwise Results (LLMBar)'\n    columns:\n    - Judge\n    - n_consistent\n    - Academic Wins\n    - Conv. Wins\n    - Win Rate\n    - Pairwise p\n    - Likert p\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - 53\n      - 35\n      - 18\n      - 66.0%\n      - 0.015*\n      - '0.289'\n    - - Claude-Sonnet\n      - 50\n      - 31\n      - 19\n      - 62.0%\n      - 0.042*\n      - '0.511'\n    - - Gemini-Flash\n      - 56\n      - 40\n      - 16\n      - 71.4%\n      - 0.003**\n      - '0.167'\n  - title: 'Table A3: Cross-Axis Summary (LLMBar, 3 judges)'\n    columns:\n    - Axis\n    - Mean WR\n    - Judges Sig. (3)\n    - NLI Pass\n    - Likert Detects?\n    rows:\n    - - Formality\n      - 68.5%\n      - 3/3\n      - 88%\n      - 0/3\n    - - Register\n      - 66.5%\n      - 3/3\n      - 86%\n      - 0/3\n    - - Tone\n      - —\n      - —\n      - 65% (failed)\n      - N/A\n    - - Verbosity\n      - —\n      - —\n      - 65% (failed)\n      - N/A\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Appendix Figure: Cross-axis bar chart。四个 axes，每个三柱 (GPT-4o, Claude, Gemini)。\n    Formality 和 Register 均高于 50% baseline，Tone 和 Verbosity 标注 \"Failed H1\"。 视觉化 CSD\n    的 axis-dependent 有效性。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Register 作为第二个 working axis 将 C3 从 \"only formality works\" 提升为 \"content-preserving\n    surface-level axes generally work\"。效应量级系统性排序 formality > register > (tone/verbosity\n    failed)，与 linguistic level 数量正相关： formality 跨词汇+句法+语用，register 跨词汇+句法，tone 主要在语用层。\n    这提供了 principled taxonomy：改变 surface form 而不改变 information content 或 epistemic\n    commitment 的 axes 适用于 CSD。\n\n    '\n- name: Non-Qwen rewriter control\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: '使用 Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct 作为替代 rewriter，对 LLMBar formality 运行完整 pipeline。\n    与 Qwen3-32B 结果比较，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。GPT-4o 作为 judge。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n    llama_nli_mean: 0.881\n    llama_bertscore_mean: 0.836\n    llama_n_consistent: 52\n    llama_formal_win_rate: 0.66\n    llama_sign_test_p: 0.015\n    qwen_nli_pass_rate: 0.88\n    qwen_formal_win_rate: 0.691\n    qwen_sign_test_p: 0.006\n    winrate_difference: 0.031\n    fisher_exact_p_for_difference: 0.42\n    rewriter_effect_significant: false\n  result_rationale: 'Llama rewriter 产生略低但仍显著的 formality premium (0.66 vs 0.69)，差异不显著\n    (Fisher p=0.42)。NLI pass rate 略低 (0.85 vs 0.88) 因为 Llama-70B 在 instruction following\n    上略弱于 Qwen3-32B (后者受益于 Qwen3 的强 instruction tuning)，导致少量 counterfactual 有轻微语义偏移。3%\n    win rate 差异在统计噪声范围内，排除了 \"Qwen rewriter 引入某种被 judge 偏好的 writing pattern\" 的 confound。\n    关键论点：formality bias 检测不依赖于特定 rewriter family。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table A4: Rewriter Ablation (GPT-4o × LLMBar, Formality)'\n    columns:\n    - Rewriter\n    - NLI Pass\n    - Formal WR\n    - Pairwise p\n    - n_consistent\n    rows:\n    - - Qwen3-32B\n      - 88%\n      - 69.1%\n      - 0.006**\n      - 55\n    - - Llama-3.1-70B\n      - 85%\n      - 66.0%\n      - 0.015*\n      - 52\n    - - Difference\n      - -3%\n      - -3.1%\n      - Fisher p=0.42\n      - —\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Appendix 级实验，但对 reviewer 质疑 rewriter choice 时提供决定性回应。 两个不同 family 的 rewriter\n    产生一致的 formality premium，确认效应的 robustness。\n\n    '\n- name: Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\n  plan_id: exp-010\n  description: 'DREAM CRITICAL。对已有 scored_32b.jsonl 数据做 sign test：每对中 formal version\n    的 Likert score 是否严格高于 casual version？如果 binarized Likert sign test 也显著 → gap 是\n    test choice 差异，非 measurement method 差异。如果不显著 → 确认 C2。 零成本重分析。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    data_source: scored_32b.jsonl (GPT-4o × LLMBar, n=88 primary)\n    n_primary: 88\n    n_formal_higher: 29\n    n_casual_higher: 21\n    n_tied: 38\n    tie_fraction: 0.432\n    n_non_tied: 50\n    binarized_formal_rate: 0.58\n    sign_test_p: 0.24\n    is_significant: false\n    strict_binarize_diff_ge2:\n      n_non_tied: 18\n      formal_wins: 11\n      sign_test_p: 0.48\n    pairwise_formal_wr: 0.691\n    pairwise_p: 0.006\n    gap_confirmed: true\n  result_rationale: 'Binarized Likert 不显著 (p=0.24) 的根因是 Likert scale 的 discretization\n    loss。 在 1-10 量表上，formality 引入的 quality perception 差异约 0.10 分 (从 Likert ATE)， 这远小于一个\n    scale step。因此 43.2% 的 pair 获得相同 Likert score (tied)——这些 pair 中 judge 确实感知到了 formality\n    差异 (pairwise 中会做出选择)，但 Likert 的 粗粒度量表无法捕捉这个差异。在 50 个 non-tied pairs 中，formal 略占优\n    (58%) 但 sample size 太小 (n=50 而非 pairwise 的 n=55 consistent)，sign test power 不足。\n    即使用更严格的 binarization (score difference ≥ 2)，n 降到 18，formal 11/18 (61%) 但 p=0.48\n    更加不显著。关键 insight: pairwise 的 forced-choice 消除了 tie 问题—— judge 必须在两个版本间选择，将 Likert\n    中被 tie 掩盖的微弱偏好显现出来。 这证明 Likert-Pairwise gap 是 measurement granularity 差异，非 statistical\n    test 选择差异。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 11: Binarized Likert vs Pairwise — C2 Decisive Test'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - n (non-tied/consistent)\n    - Formal Rate\n    - Sign Test p\n    - Conclusion\n    rows:\n    - - Pairwise (position-controlled)\n      - 55\n      - 69.1%\n      - 0.006**\n      - Significant bias detected\n    - - Binarized Likert (score > comparison)\n      - 50\n      - 58.0%\n      - '0.240'\n      - Not significant\n    - - Binarized Likert (diff ≥ 2)\n      - 18\n      - 61.1%\n      - '0.481'\n      - Not significant\n    footnote: Same underlying data (scored_32b.jsonl). Pairwise detects what binarized\n      Likert misses.\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 4 (or Figure 1 panel C): 三柱对比图。柱1: Pairwise formal rate 69.1% (显著, 深色)。\n    柱2: Binarized Likert formal rate 58.0% (不显著, 浅色)。柱3: Raw Likert ATE p=0.33 (不显著,\n    浅色)。标注 \"43% of Likert pairs tied — pairwise breaks ties\"。 这是 C2 的 visual proof。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'THIS IS THE DECISIVE EVIDENCE FOR C2。binarized_likert_sign_p = 0.24 在\n    [0.12, 1.0] 范围内。 排除了 \"Likert 和 Pairwise 用不同 statistical test 所以不可比\" 的 alternative\n    explanation。 现在三种分析都使用 sign test on binary outcome，唯一差异是 measurement method： (1)\n    Pairwise forced-choice → 69.1%, p=0.006 (2) Binarized Likert score comparison\n    → 58.0%, p=0.24 (3) Raw Likert ATE → p=0.33 Pairwise 胜出是因为它消除了 Likert 的 tie problem\n    (43% tied) 和 between-item calibration noise。 Main Result Table 中增加 Binarized Likert\n    列是 C2 的命门证据。\n\n    '\n- name: NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\n  plan_id: exp-011\n  description: '在 70%, 75%, 80%, 85%, 90%, 95% 六个 NLI threshold 上重新计算 formality pairwise\n    results。 验证结论对 threshold 选择的 robustness。零成本重分析已有 pairwise_32b 数据。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    data_source: pairwise_results_32b.jsonl (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\n    thresholds:\n      nli_70:\n        n_pairs_pass: 96\n        n_consistent: 53\n        formal_wins: 37\n        formal_wr: 0.698\n        sign_test_p: 0.005\n      nli_75:\n        n_pairs_pass: 94\n        n_consistent: 52\n        formal_wins: 36\n        formal_wr: 0.692\n        sign_test_p: 0.006\n      nli_80:\n        n_pairs_pass: 88\n        n_consistent: 50\n        formal_wins: 35\n        formal_wr: 0.7\n        sign_test_p: 0.005\n      nli_85:\n        n_pairs_pass: 72\n        n_consistent: 42\n        formal_wins: 31\n        formal_wr: 0.738\n        sign_test_p: 0.003\n      nli_90:\n        n_pairs_pass: 52\n        n_consistent: 46\n        formal_wins: 34\n        formal_wr: 0.739\n        sign_test_p: 0.002\n      nli_95:\n        n_pairs_pass: 36\n        n_consistent: 28\n        formal_wins: 21\n        formal_wr: 0.75\n        sign_test_p: 0.013\n    all_significant_70_to_95: true\n    winrate_trend: monotonically increasing (0.698 → 0.750)\n    p_value_trend: decreasing then increasing (0.005 → 0.002 → 0.013) due to n tradeoff\n    significant_range: 70%-95%\n  result_rationale: 'Formality effect 在所有 NLI threshold 上均显著，因为 formality 改写是高质量的\n    surface-level 变换——即使在宽松 threshold (70%) 下加入的额外 pairs 中有一些 semantic drift， formality\n    premium 仍然 dominant。Win rate 随 threshold 提高而单调递增 (0.698→0.750)， 说明 cleaner pairs\n    (higher NLI) 的 formality effect 更纯——content preservation 越好， observed bias 越接近\n    true causal effect。p 值在 85-90% 处最低 (0.002)，因为此处 n (42-46) 与 effect size (0.74)\n    达到最佳平衡；95% threshold 下 n 降到 28， 尽管 effect size 最高 (0.75)，power 损失导致 p 略升至 0.013，但仍远低于\n    0.05。 Tone 的 NLI 在 72% 处 borderline——sensitivity analysis 显示即使在 70% threshold\n    下 formality 仍稳健，这不是 threshold tuning 的结果。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 12: NLI Threshold Sensitivity (GPT-4o × LLMBar, Formality Pairwise)'\n    columns:\n    - NLI Threshold\n    - n_pass\n    - n_consistent\n    - Formal WR\n    - Sign Test p\n    rows:\n    - - ≥70%\n      - 96\n      - 53\n      - 69.8%\n      - 0.005**\n    - - ≥75%\n      - 94\n      - 52\n      - 69.2%\n      - 0.006**\n    - - ≥80%\n      - 88\n      - 50\n      - 70.0%\n      - 0.005**\n    - - ≥85%\n      - 72\n      - 42\n      - 73.8%\n      - 0.003**\n    - - ≥90%\n      - 52\n      - 46\n      - 73.9%\n      - 0.002**\n    - - ≥95%\n      - 36\n      - 28\n      - 75.0%\n      - 0.013*\n    footnote: 'All thresholds from 70% to 95% yield significant results. Default threshold:\n      80%.'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 4: 双 Y 轴折线图。X 轴: NLI threshold (70%-95%)。左 Y 轴 (蓝线): formal win rate，\n    缓慢上升。右 Y 轴 (红线): -log10(p)，先升后降 (n-effect size tradeoff)。 水平虚线标注 p=0.05。所有 threshold\n    点均在虚线之上。阴影区标注 \"default threshold\"。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'nli_threshold_sensitivity_significant_range = [''70%-95%'']，完美匹配核心假设。\n    结论不依赖 threshold 选择——从最宽松 (70%) 到最严格 (95%) 均显著。 Win rate 随 threshold 上升这一 monotonic\n    trend 说明 content preservation quality 与 formality effect purity 正相关，支持 CSD 的 causal\n    interpretation。\n\n    '\n- name: Consistency filter bias analysis\n  plan_id: exp-012\n  description: '比较 position-consistent pairs vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI scores、text\n    lengths、 task types，检查 42-52% 的 discard rate 是否引入系统性偏差。零成本重分析。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    data_source: pairwise_results_32b.jsonl\n    total_valid_pairs: 98\n    n_consistent: 55\n    n_inconsistent: 43\n    discard_rate: 0.439\n    consistent_nli_mean: 0.903\n    inconsistent_nli_mean: 0.886\n    nli_ttest_p: 0.42\n    nli_difference_significant: false\n    consistent_text_length_mean: 142.3\n    inconsistent_text_length_mean: 137.8\n    length_ttest_p: 0.58\n    length_difference_significant: false\n    consistent_formal_orig_fraction: 0.6\n    inconsistent_formal_orig_fraction: 0.558\n    orig_style_chi2_p: 0.67\n    orig_style_difference_significant: false\n    consistent_bertscore_mean: 0.848\n    inconsistent_bertscore_mean: 0.834\n    bertscore_ttest_p: 0.38\n    bertscore_difference_significant: false\n    task_type_chi2_p: 0.73\n    task_type_difference_significant: false\n    any_significant_difference: false\n    filter_introduces_bias: false\n  result_rationale: 'Position-consistency filtering 不引入系统性偏差，因为 position inconsistency\n    的主要来源 是 judge 的 confidence 而非 pair 的 systematic properties。Judge 对某些 pairs 有明确偏好\n    (无论位置如何都选同一个) → consistent，对另一些 pairs 犹豫不决 (位置影响选择) → inconsistent。 犹豫不决与 pair\n    的 NLI、text length、task type 无关，而与 quality 差异的微妙程度有关—— 当两个版本在 judge 眼中 \"差不多好\" 时，position\n    成为 tie-breaker。这是随机噪声， 不是对特定类型 pair 的系统性过滤。NLI 略高 (0.903 vs 0.886) 但 p=0.42 不显著，\n    说明 content preservation 质量不驱动 consistency。consistent pairs 中 formal-original fraction\n    (0.60) 略高于 inconsistent (0.56)，但差异远不显著 (p=0.67)，排除了 \"filtering selects for original-preference-aligned\n    pairs\" 的 confound。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table A5: Consistency Filter Bias Analysis (GPT-4o × LLMBar)'\n    columns:\n    - Property\n    - Consistent (n=55)\n    - Inconsistent (n=43)\n    - Test\n    - p\n    rows:\n    - - NLI Mean\n      - '0.903'\n      - '0.886'\n      - t-test\n      - '0.42'\n    - - Text Length (words)\n      - '142.3'\n      - '137.8'\n      - t-test\n      - '0.58'\n    - - BERTScore Mean\n      - '0.848'\n      - '0.834'\n      - t-test\n      - '0.38'\n    - - Formal-Original %\n      - 60.0%\n      - 55.8%\n      - χ²\n      - '0.67'\n    - - Task Type Distribution\n      - —\n      - —\n      - χ²\n      - '0.73'\n    footnote: No significant differences. Consistency filtering does not systematically\n      bias the retained sample.\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: '所有 5 个 comparison 均不显著 (最小 p=0.38)，conclusively 排除 systematic filter\n    bias。 42-52% 的 discard rate 虽高，但 discarded pairs 与 retained pairs 在 observables\n    上 indistinguishable。Reviewer 对 \"high discard rate → biased sample\" 的 concern 可用此表直接回应。建议放在\n    Appendix 作为 methodological robustness check。\n\n    '\n- name: Human NLI validation (80 annotations)\n  plan_id: exp-013\n  description: 'Human validation of NLI gate decisions。对 80 个 counterfactual pairs\n    做人工标注： content 是否 preserved。报告 human-NLI agreement (Cohen''s κ)。 可使用 LLM-as-annotator\n    (GPT-4) + human spot check 的混合策略。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_annotated: 80\n    n_nli_high: 50\n    n_nli_low: 30\n    human_preserved: 62\n    human_not_preserved: 18\n    human_preservation_rate: 0.775\n    nli_preserved: 58\n    nli_not_preserved: 22\n    both_preserved: 54\n    both_not_preserved: 14\n    nli_preserved_human_not: 4\n    nli_not_preserved_human_yes: 8\n    raw_agreement: 0.85\n    cohens_kappa: 0.72\n    kappa_interpretation: substantial agreement\n    nli_false_positive_rate: 0.069\n    nli_false_negative_rate: 0.129\n    false_positive_pattern: subtle information additions in formal rewrites that NLI\n      misses\n    false_negative_pattern: stylistic paraphrases that NLI over-penalizes as semantic\n      change\n  result_rationale: 'Cohen''s κ = 0.72 (substantial agreement) 因为 NLI 模型 (DeBERTa-large-MNLI)\n    的 training data 与 content preservation 判断高度对齐——NLI 本质上就是判断两个文本是否表达相同信息， 这与 \"counterfactual\n    是否保持 content\" 的判断完全一致。False positive rate 低 (6.9%) 说明 NLI gate 通过的 pairs 绝大多数确实\n    content-preserved——这是 CSD 结论可信度的基础。 False negative rate 较高 (12.9%) 说明 NLI 偏保守\n    (over-reject)，但这对 CSD 是安全的方向： over-rejection 意味着 retained pairs 的 content preservation\n    质量比 NLI score 建议的更高。 8 个 false negative 主要是 stylistic paraphrasing (如换用近义词或调整句子结构)\n    被 NLI 判为 non-entailment，但人工判断这些改变不影响信息内容。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table A6: Human-NLI Agreement on Content Preservation (n=80)'\n    columns:\n    - ''\n    - 'Human: Preserved'\n    - 'Human: Not Preserved'\n    - Total\n    rows:\n    - - 'NLI: Preserved (≥0.80)'\n      - 54\n      - 4\n      - 58\n    - - 'NLI: Not Preserved (<0.80)'\n      - 8\n      - 14\n      - 22\n    - - Total\n      - 62\n      - 18\n      - 80\n    footnote: Cohen's κ = 0.72 (substantial agreement). NLI FPR = 6.9%, FNR = 12.9%.\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Appendix Figure: Scatter plot，X 轴 NLI score (0-1)，Y 轴 human preservation judgment\n    (binary, jittered)。标注 threshold 垂直线在 0.80。右上象限 (both agree: preserved) 最密集，左下象限\n    (both agree: not preserved) 次之。右下 (NLI high, human not) = 4 点 标注为 false positives。展示\n    NLI score 与 human judgment 的一致性。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'κ = 0.72 在 [0.61, 0.80] \"substantial\" 范围内，满足审稿人对 NLI gate 可信度的要求。 NLI\n    偏保守 (FNR > FPR) 对 CSD 有利：retained pairs 的 content preservation 质量 被 underestimate\n    而非 overestimate。建议论文中强调：\"NLI false positives are rare (6.9%), meaning pairs that\n    pass the gate genuinely preserve content.\"\n\n    '\n- name: Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\n  plan_id: exp-014\n  description: 'Logistic regression 正式分离 formality 和 original preference。 Pool exp-001/002\n    所有 judge×benchmark pairwise 数据。DV: formal_preferred (1/0)。 IV: is_formal_original\n    (1/0), judge (fixed effects), benchmark (fixed effects)。 Test formality 主效应 (intercept)\n    是否显著，interaction 是否不显著。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    data_source: pooled pairwise from all judge × benchmark combinations\n    n_observations: 459\n    intercept_beta: 0.52\n    intercept_se: 0.19\n    intercept_z: 2.74\n    intercept_p: 0.006\n    intercept_odds_ratio: 1.68\n    intercept_interpretation: formal 被偏好的 odds 是 casual 的 1.68 倍，controlling for original\n      status\n    is_formal_original_beta: 0.34\n    is_formal_original_se: 0.17\n    is_formal_original_z: 2.0\n    is_formal_original_p: 0.046\n    is_formal_original_or: 1.4\n    interaction_beta: 0.12\n    interaction_se: 0.22\n    interaction_z: 0.55\n    interaction_p: 0.58\n    interaction_significant: false\n    judge_claude_beta: -0.28\n    judge_claude_p: 0.11\n    judge_gemini_beta: 0.19\n    judge_gemini_p: 0.24\n    benchmark_alpacaeval_beta: -0.08\n    benchmark_alpacaeval_p: 0.62\n    benchmark_mtbench_beta: -0.15\n    benchmark_mtbench_p: 0.38\n    mcfadden_r2: 0.042\n    aic: 582.3\n    bic: 611.7\n    raw_mean_formal_wr: 0.664\n    original_preference_contribution: 0.033\n    csd_adjusted_formal_wr: 0.631\n    logistic_formality_coef_p: 0.006\n  result_rationale: 'Formality 主效应 (intercept β₀=0.52, p=0.006) 显著，说明控制 original status\n    后 formal 仍被系统性偏好——这是 formality bias 作为 independent causal effect 的统计证据。 is_formal_original\n    (β₁=0.34, p=0.046) 边缘显著，说明 original preference 确实存在 但效应量 (OR=1.40) 远小于 formality\n    (OR=1.68)。关键：interaction term 不显著 (p=0.58)， 意味着 formality 的效应不依赖于 formal 版本是否为\n    original——无论 formal 是原文还是改写， judge 都偏好它。这彻底回应了 \"observed formality bias 只是 original\n    preference 的 proxy\" 的 alternative explanation。Judge 和 benchmark fixed effects\n    不显著，说明 formality premium 在不同 judge 和 benchmark 间是 stable 的 (尽管 magnitude 有差异，\n    但 direction 一致)。CSD-adjusted formal win rate = 63.1% (扣除 original preference 贡献\n    3.3 个百分点)，这是对 reviewer 最保守友好的 headline number。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 13: Logistic Regression — Formality vs Original Preference Decomposition'\n    columns:\n    - Predictor\n    - β\n    - SE\n    - z\n    - p\n    - Odds Ratio\n    rows:\n    - - Intercept (formality effect)\n      - '0.52'\n      - '0.19'\n      - '2.74'\n      - 0.006**\n      - '1.68'\n    - - is_formal_original\n      - '0.34'\n      - '0.17'\n      - '2.00'\n      - 0.046*\n      - '1.40'\n    - - Interaction\n      - '0.12'\n      - '0.22'\n      - '0.55'\n      - '0.583'\n      - '1.13'\n    - - 'Judge: Claude (vs GPT-4o)'\n      - '-0.28'\n      - '0.17'\n      - '-1.65'\n      - '0.110'\n      - '0.76'\n    - - 'Judge: Gemini (vs GPT-4o)'\n      - '0.19'\n      - '0.16'\n      - '1.19'\n      - '0.240'\n      - '1.21'\n    - - 'Bench: AlpacaEval (vs LLMBar)'\n      - '-0.08'\n      - '0.16'\n      - '-0.50'\n      - '0.620'\n      - '0.92'\n    - - 'Bench: MT-Bench (vs LLMBar)'\n      - '-0.15'\n      - '0.17'\n      - '-0.88'\n      - '0.380'\n      - '0.86'\n    footnote: N=459 observations pooled across 9 judge×benchmark combinations. McFadden\n      R²=0.042.\n  - title: 'Table 14: CSD-Adjusted Win Rate'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Value\n    - Source\n    rows:\n    - - Raw formal win rate (mean across combos)\n      - 66.4%\n      - exp-001/002\n    - - Original preference contribution\n      - +3.3%\n      - exp-014 β₁\n    - - CSD-adjusted formal win rate\n      - 63.1%\n      - Raw − original contribution\n    - - 95% CI of adjusted rate\n      - '[57.2%, 69.0%]'\n      - Bootstrap\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 5 (main): Effect decomposition waterfall chart。 Bar 1: Raw formal WR =\n    66.4%。 Bar 2: −3.3% (original preference, green downward)。 Bar 3: Net formality\n    causal effect = 63.1% (blue, 13.1% above 50% baseline)。 Error bars on final bar\n    from bootstrap CI。 Visual proof that formality effect survives original preference\n    correction。\n\n    '\n  analysis: logistic_formality_coef_p = 0.006 在 [0.001, 0.05] 范围内。Interaction p =\n    0.58 明确不显著。C4 (practical guidance) 有了统计基础：CSD-adjusted win rate 公式为 adjusted_wr\n    = raw_wr - β₁/(β₀+β₁) × (raw_wr - 0.50)。这比 ad-hoc additive correction 更有统计根据。Paper\n    可以给出 practitioner checklist：(1) use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit;\n    (2) run RATE control to quantify original preference; (3) report both raw and\n    CSD-adjusted win rates; (4) verify content preservation per axis before applying\n    CSD。\n","numLines":1292,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1292}}}
