{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NL4NEz5zd95B273sQwsMUz","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/report.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Handover — 2026-05-21\\\\n\\\\n> 由 Agent 生成，每次状态变更后自动更新。硬限 150 行。\\\\n\\\\n## 运行中\\\\n（无）\\\\n\\\\n## 待处理\\\\n- register_pilot（排队等待 GPU）\\\\n- exp014_logistic_decomposition: The observed 69.1% formal win rate in pairwise comparison is primarily driven by original-preference bias rather than genuine formality effect, and logistic regression decomposition will show formality coefficient is non-significant after controlling for original preference（排队等待 GPU）\\\\n- exp012_consistency_bias: The consistency filter (discarding 43% of pairs) introduces systematic selection bias by preferentially retaining pairs with higher NLI/BERTScore or different text characteristics, biasing downstream analysis（排队等待 GPU）\\\\n- exp011_nli_sensitivity: The 0.90 NLI threshold is on a cliff edge where small changes dramatically affect pass rate and downstream pairwise results, making our findings threshold-dependent rather than robust（排队等待 GPU）\\\\n\\\\n## 近期结论\\\\n- **exp010_binarized_likert** (success): Likert-vs-Pairwise sensitivity gap is due to measurement structure (forced choice eliminates ties) not statistical test choice; binarized Likert with sign test will remain non-significant (p>0.05) while pairwise sign test is significant (p=0.006), because 1-10 integer Likert produces excessive ties that mask the signal ← 基于 pairwise_32b\\\\n- **verbosity_32b** (negative): Verbosity axis (verbose/concise) produces stronger style bias signal than formality in GPT-4o judge: pairwise win rate ≥60% with p<0.05 and/or Likert corrected ATE with d≥0.3, because verbose responses contain more surface-level detail that judges may conflate with thoroughness ← 基于 pairwise_32b\\\\n- **tone_pilot** (negative): Tone axis (assertive/hedging) RATE counterfactuals preserve content (NLI+BERTScore pass rate ≥80%) because tone changes only modify epistemic hedging markers without altering factual claims, making it a viable third axis alongside formality ← 基于 pairwise_32b\\\\n\\\\n## 趋势\\\\n成功 2 / 负向 4 / 失败 0 / 共 6\\\\n\\\\n## 下一步\\\\n（无活跃 idea，请通过 ideas.md 添加）\\\\n\\\\n## 资源状态\\\\nwestb-29275: 无 GPU 信息\\\\n\\\\n## 告警\\\\n（无）\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 2006, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LG3r6sLLj21uQBGn4qcyPw","session_id":"e6e97501-db33-49e4-82d6-a111de115694","uuid":"7cbb61ca-c058-4395-9d6a-d96f10ff991a","timestamp":"2026-05-21T00:19:20.094Z"}
