{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EChb3iTzCsZucr3ssPmda9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: LLM Judge Style Bias — Research Landscape\n3\tdescription: 从10篇论文蒸馏的LLM-as-Judge风格偏差研究领域隐性经验：实验设计共识、方法趋势、竞品定位、研究空白\n4\ttype: research\n5\tsource_papers: 8 deep-read + 2 abstract-only (2018-2026)\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## 核心共识：Style 是 LLM Judge 的主宰偏差\n9\t\n10\tStyle-overall相关性R=0.999（SOS-Bench）；style bias 0.76-0.92远超position bias≤0.04（Soumik 2026）；style/format是preference leakage主载体（Preference Leakage ICLR'26）。**支持度：5/8，置信度：高。**\n11\t\n12\t## 标准实验设计模式\n13\t\n14\t**Judge模型覆盖**：至少3-5个异构LLM（GPT-4o + Claude + Gemini/Llama + 开源），跨provider验证是reviewer期待的最低标准。支持度：5/8，置信度：高（LC-AlpacaEval, SOS-Bench, Preference Leakage, Soumik, FairJudge）。\n15\t\n16\t**控制干预实验**：注入已知缺陷（事实错误/风格变化/特征抑制）量化judge敏感度差异，比纯相关性分析更有因果说服力。支持度：4/8，置信度：高（SOS-Bench的sarcasm/-96% vs wrong/-13%，CASSE的12×12矩阵，Soumik的controlled dataset）。\n17\t\n18\t**统计严谨性标配**：Bootstrap 95% CIs（n≥2000）+ McNemar/显著性检验 + Holm-Bonferroni多重比较校正。支持度：3/8，置信度：中（Soumik, Preference Leakage, RATE）。\n19\t\n20\t**半合成验证**：在已知ground truth的合成数据上先验证，再推广到真实数据。支持度：2/8，置信度：中（RATE的typo实验, Veitch的semi-synthetic peer review）。\n21\t\n22\t## 标准Benchmark与指标\n23\t\n24\t**Benchmark频率**：AlpacaEval/Arena-Hard（各2/8）、MT-Bench（2/8）、Chatbot Arena作为人类参考（2/8）。自建controlled dataset成为趋势（SOS-Bench 152K, Soumik 225, CASSE 12200）。\n25\t\n26\t**指标**：Win Rate（5/8）、Spearman Correlation with human（3/8）、Human Agreement（3/8）、Bias Score（2/8）、Cohen's kappa（2/8）。因果方向：ATE/Cohen's d（RATE）。\n27\t\n28\t## 方法论趋势\n29\t\n30\t**上升**：因果推断框架用于judge debiasing（LC-AlpacaEval用causal mediation，RATE用double-rewrite ATE，Counterfactual Rhetorical用Bradley-Terry）；LLM生成反事实文本作为干预工具；多维度交叉偏差分析。\n31\t\n32\t**消退**：单维度偏差分析（仅length或仅position）；无统计检验的裸数字比较；纯prompt工程debiasing（Soumik证明效果model-dependent）。\n33\t\n34\t## 竞品Claim与定位\n35\t\n36\t| 关系 | 论文 | 核心Claim |\n37\t|------|------|-----------|\n38\t| Competitor | Preference Leakage (ICLR'26) | 模型家族关系通过style泄漏偏好，contextual calibration降59%Error Bias |\n39\t| Competitor | Soumik (2026) | CoT是唯一universally safe策略，debiasing效果model-dependent |\n40\t| Competitor | FairJudge (2026) | 训练侧三阶段(SFT→DPO→GRPO)，8B超72B/671B |\n41\t| Foundation | LC-AlpacaEval (ICLR'25) | Length as causal mediator，回归去偏 |\n42\t| Foundation | SOS-Bench (ICLR'25) | Style-overall R=0.999，sarcasm/-96% vs wrong/-13% |\n43\t| Foundation | RATE (ICML'25) | Double-rewrite消除反事实系统误差 |\n44\t| Foundation | Counterfactual Rhetorical | Persona反事实+BT聚合度量修辞风格 |\n45\t| Complementary | CASSE (2026) | Style特征因果纠缠，mitigation面临alignment tax |\n46\t\n47\t## 研究空白（我们的机会）\n48\t\n49\t1. **多维Style因果分解**：现有工作要么把style当单一维度(length/整体style)，要么只做两两交互(CASSE)，无人做judge评分中多维style的联合因果分解。支持度：交叉盲区，置信度：高。\n50\t2. **Style bias × Preference leakage联合处理**：两类偏差被独立研究，无人考虑交互。置信度：中。\n51\t3. **Debiasing的下游对齐影响**：所有论文止步于\"judge更准了\"，无人验证去偏judge是否改善实际模型对齐。置信度：中。\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LG3r6sLLj21uQBGn4qcyPw","session_id":"e6e97501-db33-49e4-82d6-a111de115694","uuid":"4bee43c2-ca6c-4c3e-8669-627e745c2bd5","timestamp":"2026-05-21T00:19:48.442Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TicTvYsARuX5k88F2YHuzq","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/literature_map.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"meta:\\\\n  last_updated: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20T09:30:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n  total_papers: 10\\\\ncategories:\\\\n  - style-bias-documentation\\\\n  - judge-debiasing\\\\n  - causal-text-methods\\\\n  - evaluation-benchmarks\\\\npapers:\\\\n  sos_bench_2025:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Style Over Substance: Failure Modes of LLM Judges in Alignment Benchmarking\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Murugadoss et al.\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.15268\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: style-bias-documentation\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Largest meta-benchmark documenting style-over-substance failure in LLM judges across 152K data points. Establishes the core problem CSD addresses.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: \\\\\\\"2409.15268\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n\\\\n  preference_leakage_2026:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Preference Leakage: A Contamination Problem in LLM-as-a-judge\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Li et al.\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.01534\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: style-bias-documentation\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Shows judges rely on 'stylistic regularities—tone consistency, sentence cadence, punctuation density'. Establishes style bias propagation chain from judge → preference data → reward model → policy.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: \\\\\\\"2502.01534\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n\\\\n  fairjudge_2026:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"FairJudge: An Adaptive, Debiased, and Consistent LLM-as-a-Judge\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Wang et al.\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.06625\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: judge-debiasing\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Most directly relevant concurrent work. Trains dedicated judge via SFT→DPO→GRPO but requires retraining (white-box). CSD is black-box post-hoc—key differentiator.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: \\\\\\\"2602.06625\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n\\\\n  rate_icml_2025:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"RATE: Causal Explainability of Reward Models with Imperfect Counterfactuals\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Shen et al.\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICML 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.00000\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: causal-text-methods\\\\n    role: method-component\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Provides the double-rewrite protocol for unbiased ATE estimation under imperfect counterfactuals. CSD adopts this protocol for Stage 1 counterfactual generation.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n\\\\n  dml_chernozhukov_2018:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Double/Debiased Machine Learning for Treatment and Structural Parameters\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Chernozhukov, V.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Chetverikov, D.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Demirer, M.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Duflo, E.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Hansen, C.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Newey, W.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Robins, J.\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2018\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Econometrics Journal\\\\\\\"\\\\n    doi: \\\\\\\"10.1111/ectj.12097\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: causal-text-methods\\\\n    role: method-component\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Provides the partially linear DML framework CSD uses in Stage 2. Doubly-robust property ensures consistency if either outcome model or propensity model is correctly specified.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n\\\\n  lc_alpacaeval_2025:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Length-Controlled AlpacaEval: A Simple Way to Debias Automatic Evaluators\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Dubois et al.\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.04475\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: judge-debiasing\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Demonstrates effective post-hoc regression debiasing but only controls single dimension (length). CSD extends to multi-dimensional interventional causal identification—key baseline.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: \\\\\\\"2404.04475\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n\\\\n  casse_2026:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"A Concise Agent is Less Expert: Revealing Side Effects of Using Style Features on Conversational Agents\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"CASSE authors\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.10809\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: style-bias-documentation\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Documents cross-feature stylistic interactions across 12 style features. Shows conciseness reduces perceived expertise—supports CSD's legitimacy-aware correction design (α parameter).\\\\\\\"\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: \\\\\\\"2601.10809\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n\\\\n  counterfactual_rhetorical_2025:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Counterfactual LLM-based Framework for Measuring Rhetorical Style\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Authors\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.19908\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: causal-text-methods\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Highly similar pipeline (LLM counterfactual rewrite + statistical aggregation) but only quantifies style effects without correction. CSD completes the quantify→correct loop.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: \\\\\\\"2512.19908\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n\\\\n  soumik_2026:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Judging the Judges: A Systematic Evaluation of Bias Mitigation Strategies in LLM-as-a-Judge Pipelines\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Soumik et al.\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.23178\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: judge-debiasing\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Tests 9 debiasing strategies across 5 judges. Best strategy (combined budget) achieves +11.2pp. CSD should directly compare against this. Effect sizes 0.76-0.92 validate our premise.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: \\\\\\\"2604.23178\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n\\\\n  veitch_uai_2020:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Adapting Text Embeddings for Causal Inference\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Veitch, V.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Sridhar, D.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Blei, D.\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2020\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"UAI 2020\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.12741\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: causal-text-methods\\\\n    role: method-component\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Establishes functional intervention framework for binary text treatments satisfying positivity. Theoretical foundation for CSD's binary style axes being well-posed interventions.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: \\\\\\\"1905.12741\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 5502, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01H5X9GAUEw6oPgskzJAS1VF","session_id":"e6e97501-db33-49e4-82d6-a111de115694","uuid":"baf05e71-b433-45fb-b5ca-efca95eca3b2","timestamp":"2026-05-21T00:19:48.297Z"}
