{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N5uKNjzQSace9VsC7L8zQ2","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/decisions.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"_next_id: 20\\\\ndecisions:\\\\n- id: D001\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 14:09 UTC\\\\n  summary: '文献蒸馏审视：研究方向无需调整，CSD 填补 #1 空白（多维 style 因果分解），post-MVP 需扩展 judge/benchmark/baseline\\\\n    覆盖'\\\\n  rationale: '10 篇论文蒸馏显示：(1) 多维 style 联合因果分解是领域 #1 空白，与 CSD 核心 claim 完全对齐；(2) 竞品 claim\\\\n    无直接重叠（FairJudge=white-box, Pref Leakage=family-based, Soumik=prompt-dependent）；(3)\\\\n    同行标准要求 3-5 异构 judge + AlpacaEval/Arena-Hard/MT-Bench + Bootstrap CIs + 对比 LC-AlpacaEval\\\\n    baseline。当前 MVP 方案足够，research 阶段需按蒸馏标准扩展。'\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on: []\\\\n- id: D002\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 14:19 UTC\\\\n  summary: MVP 全量评分 + 分层分析：score 全部 100 条，按 BERTScore 阈值 0.88/0.90/0.92 分层算 ATE，不降低阈值\\\\n  rationale: 36% pass rate (BERTScore≥0.92) 偏低但 NLI 均值 0.9422 说明语义保留好。降阈值是数据操作，不如保留完整信息。全量评分\\\\n    (n=100) 保证统计 power，分层分析同时回答\\\\\\\"严格阈值下效应是否存在\\\\\\\"和\\\\\\\"宽松阈值下效应是否增强\\\\\\\"。8B H1 fail 不消耗迭代配额（ROADMAP\\\\n    规则），32B 备用。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D001\\\\n- id: D003\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 14:20 UTC\\\\n  summary: H1 content verification 改为 NLI-only gate（≥0.90），BERTScore 降为监控指标，不作为过滤条件\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 诊断：36% pass rate 的根因是 BERTScore 惩罚 style transfer 预期的词汇变化（contractions→full\\\\n    forms 等），而非内容泄漏。NLI 均值 0.9422、抽样 >0.99 证明语义保留良好。BERTScore 作为 token-level 相似度指标与\\\\n    style transfer 评估目标矛盾（改的就是 token）。Double-rewrite pass rate 更低（21/100）进一步印证。NLI-only\\\\n    gate 是度量校准（不消耗 8B 迭代配额），与 D002 全量评分兼容——primary ATE 用 NLI≥0.90 子集，secondary 按 BERTScore\\\\n    分层。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D002\\\\n- id: D004\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 14:32 UTC\\\\n  summary: 8B 初步 ATE≈0.028 不可见，归因三因素：Likert 粒度 + 8B rewriter 质量 + RATE corruption。不计入\\\\n    kill criteria，等 n=100 + 32B\\\\n  rationale: 36/100 初步数据 Cohen's d=0.055 远低于 0.3 门槛，但三个叠加因素解释了结果：(1) 83% 零差异源于 integer\\\\n    Likert 无法捕捉 sub-integer 效应；(2) 22% identical rewrites 稀释 ATE；(3) mvp_0092 RATE\\\\n    corruption 引入极端噪声。按 ROADMAP 8B fallback 规则不消耗迭代配额。行动：完成 n=100 评分、修复 RATE prompt、等\\\\n    32B (~3h) 重跑。Research 阶段须改 logprob-based scoring。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D003\\\\n- id: D005\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 14:44 UTC\\\\n  summary: 8B MVP H2 FAIL 确认（ATE=-0.04, d=-0.034），不计入 kill criteria。等 32B 重跑为正式 MVP\\\\n    判定\\\\n  rationale: n=100 全量结果：64% 零差异，5 条 corruption 离群值贡献 -19/总-4。排除后 ATE=+0.16 方向正确但不显著。失败归因：8B\\\\n    rewriter 质量 + integer Likert 粒度 + RATE corruption。按 ROADMAP 8B fallback 规则不消耗迭代配额。32B\\\\n    (61/65GB, ~3h) ready 后用修复的 prompt 重跑为正式判定。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D004\\\\n- id: D006\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 17:32 UTC\\\\n  summary: 32B MVP H2 FAIL 确认（d=0.104），消耗 kill criteria 迭代 1/2。倾向 Path A（换 verbosity\\\\n    axis）作为迭代 2/2\\\\n  rationale: 32B 结果与 8B 几乎相同（rewrite_bias -0.205 vs -0.200，corrected ATE +0.102 vs\\\\n    +0.120），证伪\\\\\\\"模型规模是瓶颈\\\\\\\"假设。rewrite_bias 不随模型变大而缩小 → 是 RATE 方法论 noise floor 或 formality\\\\n    axis 本身效应微弱。文献蒸馏显示 verbosity 是最强 style bias（LC-AlpacaEval, SOS-Bench）。换 verbosity\\\\n    axis 只改一个变量，科学上更干净，且文献强支持。等 Reviewer 审查后正式决策。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D005\\\\n- id: D007\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 17:34 UTC\\\\n  summary: 修正策略：先测 pairwise scoring 区分测量问题 vs 弱效应，再决定是否换 axis。不消耗 rewrite 迭代配额\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 指出：32B≈8B 证明模型规模不是瓶颈，但 64% 零差异可能是 integer Likert 测量分辨率问题。换 scoring\\\\n    方式（pairwise comparison）不改变 rewrite 策略，不消耗迭代 2/2 配额。如果 pairwise 在现有 formality 数据上检测到显著\\\\n    formal preference → 测量是瓶颈，formality axis 可用；如果 pairwise 仍无效 → formality 真弱，再换\\\\n    verbosity（消耗迭代 2/2）。这比直接换 axis 更有信息量，且多一次机会。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D006\\\\n- id: D008\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 17:49 UTC\\\\n  summary: Pairwise 诊断：formality 有微弱信号（57.6%, p=0.159）但混有 original preference。补跑反向\\\\n    pairwise 修复协议违规，然后转 verbosity axis（迭代 2/2）\\\\n  rationale: Pairwise 结果落入预注册缺口（55-60% 但 p>0.05）。Reviewer 分解出 ~6.7% 纯 style preference\\\\n    + ~5.5% original preference 混淆。方法论缺陷：Agent 只跑了单向 pairwise，违反双向预注册协议。补跑反向（~100\\\\n    calls）修复协议后，无论结果如何转 verbosity——formality 作为 weak axis 保留，支撑 differential decomposition\\\\n    story。继续在 formality 上投入 ROI 太低。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D007\\\\n- id: D009\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 18:16 UTC\\\\n  summary: Formality pairwise conditional PASS（69.1%, p=0.0065）。方法论验证通过，formality\\\\n    为 weak axis。立即启动 verbosity 迭代 2/2\\\\n  rationale: 双向 pairwise 一致判定 n=55，formal win 69.1%（p=0.0065），超过预注册 60% + p<0.05 门槛。NLI≥0.90\\\\n    子集更强（73.9%, p=0.0016）。Direction-adjusted 66.7% 排除 original preference 后仍显著。casual→formal\\\\n    方向不显著（54.5%, n=22 power 不足）但不否定整体结论。这证明：(1) CSD 方法论 work；(2) style bias 真实存在；(3)\\\\n    Likert 是测量瓶颈；(4) formality 是 weak axis。Verbosity 预期效应更强，作为 primary axis 进入迭代 2/2。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D008\\\\n- id: D010\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 20:55 UTC\\\\n  summary: D009 修正：Formality pairwise conditional PASS 维持，但方向不对称（78.8% vs 54.5%），original\\\\n    preference ~12.2%\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 核实发现 D009 原始方向数字错误。正确数据：formal→casual 78.8% (p=0.001, n=33),\\\\n    casual→formal 54.5% (p=0.832, n=22)。方向严重不对称——casual→formal 基本无信号。Original preference\\\\n    估计从 ~5.5% 修正为 ~12.2%（(78.8%-54.5%)/2）。但 overall 69.1% (p=0.006) 不变，方向调整后 ~66.7%\\\\n    仍超 60% 门槛，conditional PASS 结论维持。需在论文中作为 limitation 讨论方向不对称和 original preference\\\\n    confound。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: pairwise_32b\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: 'overall 69.1% p=0.006, but direction asymmetric: 78.8% vs 54.5%'\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D009\\\\n- id: D011\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 21:15 UTC\\\\n  summary: MVP 判定：Formality pairwise conditional PASS 足以进入 research 阶段；Verbosity H1\\\\n    FAIL 作为方法边界发现纳入论文\\\\n  rationale: 预注册判定逻辑明确：\\\\\\\"Verbosity FAIL + Formality pairwise cond. PASS → 单轴 MVP，scope\\\\n    受限但可行\\\\\\\"。Formality pairwise 69.1% (p=0.006) 是可复现的因果信号。Verbosity 失败（NLI 65%，根本原因是\\\\n    verbosity 改变信息量与 RATE 内容保持假设冲突）不是方法失败而是方法适用边界——这本身是有价值的 methodological insight，与\\\\n    C3（测量洞察）互补。Research 阶段需扩展：3+ judges、2+ benchmarks、测试 tone/register 等不改变信息量的 axis。Paper\\\\n    framing 以 C3（测量方法洞察）为 primary，C1（counterfactual + pairwise pipeline）为 method，C2（formality\\\\n    evidence + method boundary analysis）为 empirical。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: pairwise_32b\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: 69.1% p=0.006 conditional PASS\\\\n  - exp_id: verbosity_32b\\\\n    role: negative\\\\n    result: H1 FAIL NLI 65%, method boundary\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D009\\\\n  - D010\\\\n- id: D012\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 21:20 UTC\\\\n  summary: 采用 direction-aware NLI 修复 verbosity 验证：expansion 用 backward NLI, compression\\\\n    用 forward NLI\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 分析发现 verbosity H1 FAIL (65%) 根因是 bidirectional NLI = min(fwd,\\\\n    bwd) 与信息量变化操作结构性不兼容。Concise→verbose 46.3% 但 verbose→concise 87.0%。Forward NLI\\\\n    对 expansion 必然失败（短文本不能蕴涵长文本新增信息），这是 NLI 的正确行为而非 bug。Direction-aware NLI 修正方法论上合理：两个方向都测\\\\\\\"大文本蕴涵小文本\\\\\\\"，是内容保持的正确语义。代码改动\\\\n    ~10 行，重跑 ~5-10 min。这是验证方法修正，不是 rewrite 策略迭代（不消耗 kill criteria）。如果修复后 verbosity\\\\n    H1 通过，可恢复双轴 story。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: verbosity_32b\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: H1 FAIL due to verification method mismatch, not rewrite quality. verbose→concise\\\\n      87% with bidirectional NLI.\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D011\\\\n- id: D013\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 21:42 UTC\\\\n  summary: Verbosity 轴使用 NLI-only gating（去掉 BERTScore 门控），direction-aware NLI 86%\\\\n    pass rate 恢复 H1\\\\n  rationale: Direction-aware NLI 将 verbosity H1 从 65% 恢复到 86%（>80% 阈值）。BERTScore 对\\\\n    verbosity 结构性不适用：expansion 方向 BERTScore 均值仅 0.6732（token-level 对齐对长度变化极其敏感），即使降阈值到\\\\n    0.70 也只有 63%。这与 D003（formality 已将 BERTScore 降为 monitoring）一致。NLI 衡量语义蕴含，BERTScore\\\\n    衡量表面形式相似度——对改变表面形式但保留语义的 style transfer，NLI 是正确的验证工具。论文中可作为 axis-adaptive verification\\\\n    方法论贡献。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: verbosity_32b\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: Direction-aware NLI 86% pass (v1 bidirectional was 65%). BERTScore ≥0.92\\\\n      only 3%, structurally incompatible with length changes.\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D012\\\\n  - D003\\\\n- id: D014\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 23:29 UTC\\\\n  summary: Tone axis pilot FAIL (NLI 65%, joint 45%)；作为 C3 方法边界证据。追加 register pilot\\\\n    测试第三个 surface axis\\\\n  rationale: Tone axis 的 assertive→hedging 方向改变认知承诺（epistemic commitment），NLI 正确识别为非蕴含。这是结构性问题，与\\\\n    formality（表面 register）和 verbosity（信息量，可用 direction-aware NLI 适配）本质不同。三轴形成清晰可行性梯度：formality\\\\n    88% > verbosity 86% > tone 45%，这本身支撑 C3（axis-dependent）。主计划采用 formality + verbosity\\\\n    两轴，tone 作为 negative control。但 register（academic/conversational）可能更接近 formality\\\\n    特性，追加 20 样本 pilot（成本极低）测试是否可作为第三个 working axis。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-004\\\\n    role: negative\\\\n    result: 'Tone pilot: NLI 65%, joint gate 45%, bimodal with 6/20 catastrophic failures'\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D013\\\\n- id: D015\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 23:33 UTC\\\\n  summary: Dream 1 三档均 3.0/6 (Findings)：修正 title/framing/claims，新增 5 个零成本实验（exp-010~014），需\\\\n    re-dream 验证\\\\n  rationale: Dream (dream_20260520T211832) 三档一致评分 3.0/6，低于目标（best≥4.0, median≥3.5）。结构性问题（不因数据好坏改变）：(1)\\\\n    \\\\\\\"decomposition/framework\\\\\\\" 过度承诺 → 改 title 和 C1/C3 表述；(2) C2 有 test-choice confound\\\\n    → 新增 exp-010 binarized Likert sign test (P0)；(3) detection-only 无 correction →\\\\n    新增 C4 practical guidance；(4) bibliography 10 refs too thin → 目标 25+；(5) original\\\\n    preference control 只在 GPT-4o×LLMBar → exp-005 扩展 scope；(6) 缺 NLI sensitivity analysis\\\\n    / consistency filter analysis / human validation → exp-011~013。修改后需 re-dream 验证达标后才批准\\\\n    P0。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: dream_20260520T211832\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: best 3.0, median 3.0, worst 3.0 — all Findings level\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D014\\\\n- id: D016\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 23:45 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'exp-010 PASS: Binarized Likert sign test confirms C2 (Likert Blindspot\\\\n    is measurement method difference, not test-choice confound)'\\\\n  rationale: 'Binarized Likert (same sign test as pairwise): NLI≥0.9 subset 60.6%\\\\n    p=0.296 vs Pairwise 69.1% p=0.006. Two-layer Likert weakness: (1) 37.5% non-tied\\\\n    vs 56.1% consistent (integer granularity creates ties), (2) weaker signal even\\\\n    among non-tied (60.6% vs 69.1%). RC2 (Dream test-choice confound concern) eliminated.\\\\n    Zero cost reanalysis.'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-010\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: 'PASS: binarized Likert p=0.296, pairwise p=0.006 on same sign test'\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D015\\\\n- id: D017\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 23:58 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'exp-011/012/014 全部 SUCCESS: NLI threshold robust, consistency filter unbiased,\\\\n    logistic decomposition confirms formality OR=2.21 (p=0.011) after controlling\\\\n    original preference'\\\\n  rationale: 'exp-011: NLI 0.70-0.95 范围内 pairwise win rate 稳定 72-74%, all p<0.005.\\\\n    双峰分布意味着阈值选择无 cliff edge. exp-012: consistent vs inconsistent pairs 无系统差异 (all\\\\n    MWU p>0.12, KS p=0.68). exp-014: Logistic regression with formality + original_pref\\\\n    + position → formality OR=2.21 p=0.011, original_pref OR=1.81 p=0.048. 替代 ad-hoc\\\\n    additive correction (Dream 三档一致批评). casual→formal subset 54.5% 符合两效应对冲预期.'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-011\\\\n    role: robustness\\\\n    result: 'SUCCESS: threshold insensitive'\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-012\\\\n    role: robustness\\\\n    result: 'SUCCESS: no filter bias'\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-014\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: 'SUCCESS: formality OR=2.21 p=0.011 after controlling original preference'\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D015\\\\n  - D016\\\\n- id: D018\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 00:11 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'exp-014 pair-level bootstrap/GEE fix confirmed: formality OR=2.21 p=0.010\\\\n    (significant), original preference OR=1.82 p=0.052 (not significant)'\\\\n  rationale: 'Independence violation (M005) fixed: paired data (98 pairs × 2 trials)\\\\n    now uses pair-level bootstrap and GEE with exchangeable correlation. Both methods\\\\n    agree closely. Formality effect barely changed (p=0.011→0.010-0.012), confirming\\\\n    robustness. Original preference crosses significance threshold (p=0.048→0.052-0.064,\\\\n    OR CI includes 1). Paper implications: formality bias is real and robust; original\\\\n    preference is suggestive but not statistically proven. Reviewer PASS.'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-014\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: formality OR=2.21 p=0.010 GEE (significant), original_pref OR=1.82 p=0.052\\\\n      GEE (not significant)\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D017\\\\n- id: D019\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 00:15 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'Register pilot: NLI-only 95% PASS (19/20), joint gate 20% FAIL. Adopt\\\\n    NLI-only gating for register (same as verbosity D013). Register-formality 50%\\\\n    agreement confirms orthogonality.'\\\\n  rationale: BERTScore ≥0.92 only 20% pass for register (mean 0.8458) because register\\\\n    rewriting changes vocabulary/syntax. NLI confirms 95% semantic preservation. Same\\\\n    pattern as verbosity (D013). Register-formality 50% agreement refutes Dream reviewer\\\\n    concern about axis overlap (r≈0.7 speculation). C3 now has 3 viable axes (formality\\\\n    88%, verbosity 86%, register 95% all NLI-only) + 1 structural failure (tone 65%).\\\\n    Register full pipeline awaits API key recovery.\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-008\\\\n    role: pilot\\\\n    result: NLI-only 95% PASS, joint gate 20% FAIL, register-formality orthogonal\\\\n      (50%)\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D013\\\\n  - D014\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 12598, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01H5X9GAUEw6oPgskzJAS1VF","session_id":"e6e97501-db33-49e4-82d6-a111de115694","uuid":"a6c2b918-4c94-47d7-b9c5-0a820ba2e57d","timestamp":"2026-05-21T00:20:08.809Z"}
